<node id="&quot;COMPLIANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compliance involves adhering to the laws and regulations governing mortgage loans, ensuring that all parties act within legal frameworks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Compliance refers to the industry standards and regulations that govern mortgage loan process and eligibility criteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8552c190e01cd6c887d540f68372a1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 52}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 313}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNDERWRITING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Underwriting is the examination and evaluation of a Borrower's creditworthiness and the sufficiency of the Mortgaged Property for the purpose of determining loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting is the process by which an institution evaluates the creditworthiness of a borrower and the risk of loan issuance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting is the process by which lenders assess the risk of lending to a borrower, evaluating their financial information and the loan terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting is the process involved in assessing and validating the borrower's documentation for loan approval, a critical step in the lending process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting is the process of evaluating the risk of insuring or lending money to a borrower based on various factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting refers to the process of evaluating a borrower's creditworthiness and the associated risks of the loan, which influences escrow waiver approvals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting is the process of evaluating a loan applicant's creditworthiness and the risk associated with the loan, critical in determining loan approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting is the process of evaluating a borrower's eligibility and risk profile for loan approval based on specific criteria and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting refers to the process by which Flagstar evaluates and approves loans, impacting the early payment default rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting is the process of evaluating the risk of insuring a loan, assessing the Borrower's creditworthiness and ability to repay."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b2fbf5161dc5c6670b7fd7548d822a73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f18d8da3052c73dc1f9fa6e9aef1a14e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc9e5323cf1da974f74cdcad0aebf55d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae2131097a3957a665d280c4ed013cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a577e8766cf4f0e1ae599795cd9c6fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1afd5d25f6f318da0cbe2e55f0a46af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0908ef3e42a9d0bcd40742960e19dbf2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 496}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 827}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrowers are individuals applying for a loan, who are required to sign the Uniform Residential Loan Application and other pertinent documents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals eligible to apply for a Home Equity Line of Credit, impacted by various eligibility criteria and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals or entities that take on a mortgage to finance the purchase of property, subject to various title insurance conditions and restrictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals or entities that take out a loan against a property, generally needing title insurance coverage to protect their financial interests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals or entities that take out loans, particularly Higher Priced Mortgage Loans in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals who apply for loans, providing necessary documentation of their financial history and current obligations when seeking mortgage refinancing or new loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals who apply for and receive loans, pledging to pay back the borrowed amount according to the agreed terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals seeking loans to finance home purchases or refinances, specifically under the Home Possible lending guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals who qualify for a Home Equity Line of Credit (HELOC) and are responsible for managing their housing expenses and debt ratio calculations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals or entities that apply for FHA loans to purchase or refinance properties, subject to eligibility requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrowers are individuals or entities that take out loans from lenders with the promise to repay the amount borrowed plus interest over a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a8254e91bb361353c2efd5fd41f17e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970955acc105f7936d7b684983cc4b58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb4e4bbf1091286e7015a8784c37cbc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f5452ea8c1afd9252c54573e518675e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4823f54b9e7afeaec0c69de7747fd4e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 152}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 616}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INELIGIBLE PRODUCTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ineligible Products are loans that do not meet the criteria to be classified as Higher Priced Mortgage Loans (HPML)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 152}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 617}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SYSTEM RESTRICTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"System Restrictions refer to limitations imposed by the Loantrac system based on the characteristics of mortgage loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 121}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;POLICIES AND PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Policies and Procedures detail the guidelines and rules governing the processing and approval of Higher Priced Mortgage Loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Policies and Procedures outlines the regulations and guidelines for loan assessment in mortgage lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"Policies and Procedures refers to the formal directives for practices guiding the management and processing of loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Policies and Procedures represent the rules and guidelines that govern the operations of the title insurance industry, specifically around handling survey exceptions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Policies and Procedures refers to the established protocols documented for the appraisal industry, suggesting structured operational guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Policies and Procedures represent the official guidelines and regulations governing the appraisal process, ensuring quality and compliance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Policies and Procedures encompass the guidelines that govern the collection of early payment default fees and the related financial operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Policies and Procedures refer to the guidelines and rules set by Flagstar Bank for managing loan processes and customer requests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Policies and Procedures refers to a set of guidelines outlined in Document #4023 that governs the handling of requests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Policies and Procedures refer to the set of regulations and guidelines that govern the loan underwriting and processing activities at Flagstar Bank."&lt;SEP&gt;"Policies and Procedures refer to the guidelines that govern the fee structures and loan underwriting processes at Flagstar."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1451e00f0a33296b7172a8a2f00a036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81cc653b56446bb1cb4eb76691010c73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e91d1878db3c593f090cf301ec4048a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6baa5293c454b23773beb478dc4d7a71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae2131097a3957a665d280c4ed013cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662a2c10d200da7291e0212d33749544&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ad59fd9fe05a2fd14af3e367ff950d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33b3eb25dce726e663be548f3764d0e0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 52}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 312}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CORRESPONDENT LOCK-IN DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Correspondent Lock-In Date is a specific date that corresponds with mortgage rate locking as confirmed by correspondents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FUNDING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Funding refers to the process of disbursing money for loans, triggering related terms and conditions associated with such transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Funding refers to the process of providing financial support for loans once they meet eligibility and processing criteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2d9f6b5b471373ca78f75c11d02725</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 119}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLOSING DOCUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Closing Documents are legal papers that finalize a real estate transaction, including details about the loan and the terms of sale."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Documents are the official paperwork required to finalize a real estate transaction, ensuring that all legalities are observed before transfer of ownership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Documents are various legal documents that need to be signed during the loan closing to complete the transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Documents refer to the paperwork required to finalize mortgage loans, ensuring all details are in compliance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Documents refer to the necessary paperwork required for finalizing a HELOC transaction, including various riders and agreements specific to the loan type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing documents for HELOCs must only include fees listed in Exhibit B, ensuring compliance and transparency in financial dealings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Documents are the legal papers required to finalize a mortgage, which can be ordered through Flagstar's Web-Based Closing Docs service."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Documents are the legal papers prepared and signed during a real estate transaction that finalize the loan and property transfer."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6a2fe6bde08b88616e4d4932fe5f5e5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717a880d45de770514dc0429a3dc79f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dcf3f3e40f27441645f474e46347d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eec7e8fc248456d980c970b75e0fbf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdba698a5ff7dd259797f2300b8f4759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 115}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 512}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLEAR TO CLOSE STATUS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Clear to Close Status indicates that a loan has been approved and is ready for funding and closing procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Clear to Close Status indicates that all necessary documents and conditions for a mortgage loan have been satisfied, and the loan is ready for funding."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 115}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 515}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ERROR MESSAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Error Message refers to alerts generated by the Loantrac system when discrepancies about loan eligibility arise."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 121}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RATE LOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rate Lock is a process that ensures a borrower secures an interest rate for a specified period during the mortgage application process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 464}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HPML&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HPML stands for Higher Priced Mortgage Loan, a classification that indicates specific compliance requirements for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPML stands for Higher Priced Mortgage Loan, indicating mortgages that come with higher interest rates and are closely monitored for compliance with federal standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"HPML stands for Higher Priced Mortgage Loans, which are consumer loans secured by a principal dwelling with specified interest rate thresholds."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 505}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSUMER-PURPOSE LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Consumer-purpose Loans are loans intended for individual consumers rather than businesses, often used for personal expenses."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBORDINATE-LIEN LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subordinate-lien Loans are secondary loans secured against a property, which have lower priority compared to primary loans in the event of default."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LENDER CREDITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lender Credits refer to funds provided by a lender to cover closing costs, often used to assist borrowers in financing the cost of their loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 121}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELIGIBLE PRODUCTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Eligible Products are loans or mortgage options that meet criteria to qualify as Higher Priced Mortgage Loans (HPML)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUSTABLE RATE MORTGAGE (ARM)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjustable Rate Mortgage (ARM) is a loan product with an interest rate that may change over the life of the loan according to market conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustable Rate Mortgage (ARM) is a mortgage type where the interest rate may change periodically based on changes in a corresponding financial index, potentially leading to fluctuating monthly payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustable Rate Mortgage (ARM) is a type of mortgage where the interest rate may change periodically based on changes in a corresponding financial index."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustable Rate Mortgages (ARMs) are loan products that have interest rates that can change periodically, based on market conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a72060811d2de811b03ec94848dcad94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3310e925ce8d483d790951bc5b7e818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 480}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTIONAL LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conventional Loans are mortgage loans that are not insured or guaranteed by the federal government and typically follow the guidelines set by Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Loans are mortgage loans that are not insured or guaranteed by the government, often having stricter eligibility criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional loans are types of mortgage loans that are not insured or guaranteed by the federal government, and they conform to specific guidelines set by Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Loans are mortgage loans that are not insured or guaranteed by the federal government, often conforming to certain guidelines for funding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Loans are standard mortgage loans that adhere to the guidelines set by Fannie Mae or Freddie Mac, with distinct fees for early payoff."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Loans are mortgages that are not directly backed by a government agency, requiring a higher credit score and down payment from borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Loans are types of loans provided by Flagstar that have specific early payoff penalties associated with them."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe4b9e8302b8de2d8d692106e4e284ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2d9f6b5b471373ca78f75c11d02725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717a880d45de770514dc0429a3dc79f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662a2c10d200da7291e0212d33749544</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 116}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 518}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 830}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REFINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Refinance is an event where existing debt obligations are replaced with new debt obligations under different terms, often to benefit from lower interest rates or to alter loan duration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refinance is the process of obtaining a new mortgage to replace an existing one, often to secure a better interest rate or different terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refinance is the process of obtaining a new mortgage to replace an existing one, often to secure better terms or lower payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refinance is the process of replacing an existing loan with a new loan, typically with better rates or terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refinance refers to the process of obtaining a new mortgage to replace an existing loan, often to benefit from better rates or terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refinance is the process of obtaining a new loan to pay off an existing loan, typically to benefit from better terms or rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Refinance refers to the process of replacing an existing mortgage with a new one, often to secure better terms or extract equity."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b06bf2c39f8da79b3399842638c80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb4e4bbf1091286e7015a8784c37cbc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 336}]</data>
</node>
