<node id="&quot;INTEREST RATE LOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest Rate Lock is a provision allowing borrowers to secure a specific interest rate for a defined time to protect against rate increases prior to loan closing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Rate Lock is an agreement between a borrower and a lender to secure a specified interest rate for a set period during the loan process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Rate Lock refers to the process of securing a mortgage interest rate for a defined period, preventing fluctuations during closing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de34030d71ef2c627010a089db20697c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123</data>
