<node id="&quot;LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Loan is a financial product where a borrower receives funds from a lender with the agreement to pay it back with interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"A loan is a financial agreement where money is borrowed and expected to be paid back with interest, crucial in residential mortgage transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to a sum of money borrowed that is expected to be paid back with interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to the financial agreement being sought by the borrower from financial institutions based on extensive criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to financial products offered to Borrowers, which may undergo the Hybrid eClose process if they meet eligibility requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to a sum of money lent to a borrower under the condition of repayment, often associated with specific terms, interest rates, and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to borrowed money that must be repaid, subject to specific requirements and guidelines in lending practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to the financial agreement where a lender provides funds to a borrower with an expectation of repayment under specified terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to the financial product being locked and extended as per the policies outlined in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to the financial product being offered by Flagstar to Borrowers, which involves a sequence of monthly payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Loan refers to the financial product that allows the buyer to purchase property, involving terms that are documented in the closing process."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Loan refers to the amount of money borrowed by the Borrower from the lender, which is expected to be paid back with interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to the amount of money borrowed from Flagstar Bank that may require repayment under specific terms and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to the amount of money borrowed to be paid back with interest over time, commonly used for purchasing property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to the financial agreement whereby a borrower receives funds for purchasing property, which is central to the matrix discussed."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Loan is a sum of money that is borrowed and expected to be paid back with interest, often used for purchasing homes or vehicles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan refers to a financial agreement allowing a borrower to receive funds under specific terms and repayment conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fff6b81ef8a66ecc49bb49ef81869a5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f18d8da3052c73dc1f9fa6e9aef1a14e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9eec682fb4dbe92270f8b8c48a9354&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d99ce4642f1e6e8c39678043a90b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780584b6e27004b17c25020078807812&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aade21d11a3ffb0d61652426f005667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6baa5293c454b23773beb478dc4d7a71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25a82bf13c8c6a8ef98d1a15a5361ea9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de34030d71ef2c627010a089db20697c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae2131097a3957a665d280c4ed013cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662a2c10d200da7291e0212d33749544&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf7af26dea16d8bcfcc9a3324ded2bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f639d102461efe890e188cbc182dba52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1afd5d25f6f318da0cbe2e55f0a46af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7240c801a08e04a5a9db69a7879361cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6589af60d5cd7b7c6c55232071772b8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 43}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 285}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 779}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Mortgage is a financial agreement in which a borrower's interest in real estate serves as collateral for a loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Mortgage is a legal instrument pledging real estate as security for the repayment of a loan, typically involving a borrower and a lending institution."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Mortgage is a loan secured by real property, which involves regular repayments over a specified period, often tied to housing events and refinancing scenarios."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage is a type of loan specifically used to purchase real estate, where the property serves as collateral."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mortgage is a financial product designed to assist individuals in purchasing real estate by providing a loan that is secured against the property being acquired."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mortgage is a type of loan specifically used to purchase real estate, where the property itself serves as collateral for the loan, typically requiring the borrower to make regular payments over a specified term until the loan is repaid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage is a legal document used in the transaction of securing a loan against a property, involved in the closing process."&lt;SEP&gt;"A mortgage is a loan specifically used to purchase real estate, which is subject to the conditions set by the title insurance policy in relation to surveys."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage is a legal agreement in which a borrower pledges property as security for a loan, typically involving title insurance requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage represents a financial agreement for property purchase that is influenced by various title insurance policies and practices described in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage is a financial instrument that allows individuals to borrow funds for purchasing real estate, secured by the property itself."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage is a loan specifically for purchasing real estate, where the property itself serves as collateral."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage refers to the financial instrument used to purchase property, with various components like interest rates and borrower qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage is a financial industry segment that deals with loans secured by real estate, specifically for purchasing property or refinancing existing mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage refers to a financial industry segment that deals with loans secured by real estate, specifically for purchasing property or refinancing existing mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage is a loan specifically secured by real estate, indicating the Borrower's obligation to repay under agreed-upon terms and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b42b071e6198f2a53344eeed3e0dca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9eec682fb4dbe92270f8b8c48a9354&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-283d5323d92a66b703dacfb0b3c98a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e91d1878db3c593f090cf301ec4048a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6baa5293c454b23773beb478dc4d7a71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970955acc105f7936d7b684983cc4b58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8552c190e01cd6c887d540f68372a1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12641cd1a4c93cf93c1aa31082da47b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7de83587d951a7ec74fcb94d81a7df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb4e4bbf1091286e7015a8784c37cbc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4823f54b9e7afeaec0c69de7747fd4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a40aeeabaca2a4a97b1dd8ad35ab142e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 106}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 471}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VA INTEREST RATE REDUCTION REFINANCE LOAN (IRRRL)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The VA Interest Rate Reduction Refinance Loan (IRRRL) is a VA-guaranteed loan designed for refinancing existing VA loans, typically at a lower interest rate, offering reduced principal and interest payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"The VA Interest Rate Reduction Refinance Loan (IRRRL) is a specific refinancing option available for borrowers wishing to refinance an existing VA loan with the goal of achieving better rates or terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b06bf2c39f8da79b3399842638c80b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 484}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIXED-RATE MORTGAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fixed-Rate Mortgages are loan products offered under the IRRRL program that include various term lengths such as 10, 15, 20, 25, and 30 years."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fixed-Rate Mortgages are loans with an interest rate that remains the same throughout the life of the loan, providing stability in monthly payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 107}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 475}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 820}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADJUSTABLE-RATE MORTGAGES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjustable-Rate Mortgages (ARMs) are loans where the interest rate may change periodically based on changes in a corresponding financial index, typically resulting in lower initial payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustable-Rate Mortgages are loan products that combine traditional and jumbo loan amounts, providing options like 5/1 CMT, but exclude manufactured homes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 107}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 475}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 820}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HUD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HUD is the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, responsible for overseeing and managing the Credit Alert Interactive Voice Response System (CAIVRS) used in the IRRRL process."&lt;SEP&gt;"HUD, the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, oversees various housing-related programs, including the IRRRL process and manages the Credit Alert Interactive Voice Response System (CAIVRS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) is a government agency that oversees housing-related programs and initiatives, including the management of the IRRRL process and CAIVRS."&lt;SEP&gt;"HUD refers to the Department of Housing and Urban Development, a U.S. government agency focused on national housing policies."&lt;SEP&gt;"HUD refers to the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, overseeing various housing and urban development programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"HUD refers to the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development, which oversees various housing initiatives and financing regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) is a government agency responsible for national policies and programs related to housing and urban development."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) is a government agency tasked with national policies and programs that address America's housing needs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) is a government agency that oversees federal programs related to housing, including the Federal Housing Administration (FHA), which manages and insures mortgage loans in the United States."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD) is a government organization that oversees federal housing programs and ensures equal housing opportunities for all Americans, providing guidance on FHA loans and regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12641cd1a4c93cf93c1aa31082da47b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7de83587d951a7ec74fcb94d81a7df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75126918f0820581a7405cbda1984bbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdba698a5ff7dd259797f2300b8f4759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 148}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 599}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLAGSTAR BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">FLAGSTAR BANK, N.A. is a financial institution based in Troy, Michigan, known for specializing in mortgage lending, offering a variety of loan programs including FHA, VA, and GRH loans. They provide services such as loan registration, locking processes, and managing rates and price quotes. FLAGSTAR BANK is involved in setting specific policies for loan registration and delivery, as well as managing loan processes. They also review community second programs for eligibility, provide guidelines for closing documentation and survey exceptions in title insurance. Additionally, FLAGSTAR BANK offers banking services, including Home Equity Lines of Credit (HELOC) transactions, and handles various loan types with associated fees for real estate financing. Overall, FLAGSTAR BANK is a prominent financial institution catering to both individual and commercial clients with a focus on mortgage loans and other financial services.</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd1c976503db6a0b9762d63aba656cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b722d926669aa7676c36ecbb75a4a233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-060d3305d5697520404f94c4fcd2cb85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662a2c10d200da7291e0212d33749544&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4823f54b9e7afeaec0c69de7747fd4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0908ef3e42a9d0bcd40742960e19dbf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e572c9b9bd53e500c5e02283f3230e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4b9e8302b8de2d8d692106e4e284ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2d9f6b5b471373ca78f75c11d02725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97d5fa1f48d7b9516a9e1f71b87048e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eec7e8fc248456d980c970b75e0fbf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1418f5447a956615e29938e7c6f0f71a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1afd5d25f6f318da0cbe2e55f0a46af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a48a482a40438f89f44e8758608310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77f9a0c774af974e032ea5bf1841d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df57131d49eba22a5ca15cafeb404cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11f5ef3fffef89b593ca081411d1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c6c6dd97681ba9caa6c83d8ddf9ec59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73179b73b8a774ced8d562931d514540&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdba698a5ff7dd259797f2300b8f4759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f642eb6cc44e3fc724fd1b5beeccd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e91d1878db3c593f090cf301ec4048a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a403e885ce18327dd600e7521b66a2e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a577e8766cf4f0e1ae599795cd9c6fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f29d1e5fffab173b878a2ce71c0888</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 496}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 828}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VA PAMPHLET 26-7&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"VA Pamphlet 26-7 is a key document that contains information and guidelines on eligibility, benefits, and loan types associated with VA loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"VA Pamphlet 26-7 provides guidelines and regulations relevant to VA loans, including the IRRRL program and borrower eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01039c48e44ce5e4ea96c87117f23d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 487}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VA FUNDING FEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The VA Funding Fee is a fee collected by the VA on each loan to cover potential losses and defaults, currently set at 0.5% for IRRRL loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The VA Funding Fee is a mandatory fee that most veterans pay when obtaining a mortgage, which can be financed or paid by the borrower or seller."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3310e925ce8d483d790951bc5b7e818</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 486}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT ALERT INTERACTIVE VOICE RESPONSE SYSTEM (CAIVRS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CAIVRS is a screening system used by FHA to ensure that borrowers do not have delinquent federal debts before loan approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"CAIVRS is a system used for screening borrowers to check for loans that are delinquent or in default, critical for the IRRRL process."&lt;SEP&gt;"CAIVRS is a system used to screen borrowers before FHA insures a loan, ensuring they are not delinquent on federal debts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d10b59eabaab0b4bdac98f88233ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 433}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPUTATION WORKSHEET&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Computation Worksheet is a document required for submitting applications for the IRRRL, detailing necessary information for processing the loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 436}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEMPORARY BUYDOWNS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Temporary Buydowns are a financing strategy that reduces the interest rate on a loan temporarily, but are noted as not eligible in the context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns are a method of reducing initial mortgage payments, though they are explicitly stated as not eligible in this document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns refer to a financing arrangement in which the interest rate is reduced for an initial period, but are not eligible under the IRRRL program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns refer to a situation where the borrower pays a reduced rate of interest for a temporary period, but in the context of this document, these are not eligible under the IRRRL program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns refer to loans structured to lower initial monthly payments for a limited period, which in this case have been stated as not eligible."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns are financing arrangements that allow for reduced interest payments for a limited period, which are typically not allowed under One-Close Construction loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns refer to arrangements that lower the borrower's mortgage rate for a temporary period during the early years of the loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns are financing arrangements that lower the interest rate on a mortgage for a specified period, typically to assist borrowers with lower initial payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns refer to special financing arrangements that temporarily reduce a borrower's interest rate during the initial years of a mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns refer to a mortgage financing arrangement where the interest rate is reduced for the initial period of the loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns refer to financing options that temporarily reduce the interest rate on a mortgage, noted as not eligible in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temporary Buydowns are financing arrangements that temporarily reduce an interest rate on a mortgage for a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-27bd5ad2c70145086339257520820a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1418f5447a956615e29938e7c6f0f71a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELIGIBILITY GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Eligibility Guidelines provide specific criteria regarding which types of properties, borrowers, and loan amounts are eligible for the IRRRL program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Guidelines refer to the specific rules and regulations that dictate what types of properties and borrowers qualify for mortgage loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Guidelines refer to the specific rules and criteria that determine whether a borrower qualifies for a particular mortgage insurance product."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6de80860713bbcd40afb3b3b69d1945f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 487}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VA REGIONAL OFFICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The VA Regional Office is the location where certain IRRRL loans, particularly those over 30 days past due, must be processed and closed with prior approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 487}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDOMINIUMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Condominiums are types of eligible properties specified in the VA IRRRL guidelines that can be financed under the program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condominiums refer to a specific type of residential property eligible for VA loans, subject to the guidelines outlined in VA Pamphlet 26-7."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01039c48e44ce5e4ea96c87117f23d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 483}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PUDs, or Planned Unit Developments, are a type of property that may qualify for VA loans, as referenced in the loan guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planned Unit Developments (PUDs) are also listed as eligible property types for financing under the VA IRRRL program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01039c48e44ce5e4ea96c87117f23d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 483}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANUFACTURED HOMES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROPERTY TYPE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Manufactured Homes are a category of homes that can qualify for VA loans if they meet specific criteria outlined in the guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes refer to homes that may be financed under the IRRRL program, though specific restrictions apply regarding eligibility, primarily for fixed-rate products only."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured homes refer to housing that is constructed off-site and can be transported; they are eligible for certain refinancing options under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes refer to homes built in factories and moved to a permanent site, subject to specific guidelines for financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes are factory-built homes that may have different financing eligibility compared to traditional real estate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes refer to homes that are built off-site and trucked to their location, which are ineligible for financing under certain conventional mortgage programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured homes are factory-built homes that are often subject to specific lending and eligibility requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manufactured Homes are structures that are built on a permanent chassis and can be transported, but are typically not eligible for certain loan types like HomeReady."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01039c48e44ce5e4ea96c87117f23d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 359}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SINGLE WIDE MANUFACTURED HOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Single Wide Manufactured Homes are specified as ineligible for financing under the VA IRRRL program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 360}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COOPERATIVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A cooperative is an ineligible property type for FHA financing, meaning loans cannot be issued for purchasing these kinds of homes under the program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cooperatives are noted as ineligible property types under the VA IRRRL program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d10b59eabaab0b4bdac98f88233ce6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 360}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORKING FARM, RANCH OR ORCHARD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Working Farm, Ranch or Orchard are types of properties excluded from VA loan eligibility under current guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Working Farms, Ranches, or Orchards are identified as ineligible properties for the VA IRRRL program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01039c48e44ce5e4ea96c87117f23d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 360}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VA LENDER'S HANDBOOK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The VA Lender's Handbook contains essential guidelines and instructions for VA loans, including underwriting requirements for the IRRRL program."&lt;SEP&gt;"The VA Lender's Handbook is a comprehensive guide issued by the Veterans Administration that outlines the guidelines and requirements for lenders offering VA loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"VA Lender's Handbook provides comprehensive guidelines and standards that lenders must follow when processing VA loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b06bf2c39f8da79b3399842638c80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01039c48e44ce5e4ea96c87117f23d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 487}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN AMOUNTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Amounts refer to the established limits and conditions for various loan products mentioned in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Amounts refer to the total financing amount that can be approved under the IRRRL program, not exceeding specific limits set by the VA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Amounts refers to the specified ranges for loans in terms of minimum and maximum financing available."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Amounts refer to the total sum of money that one borrows, which is subject to specific limits based on property types and borrower qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Amounts refers to the specified minimum and maximum sums that borrowers can access under various lending programs for specific types of properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Amounts refer to the specific quantity of money that can be borrowed as per the stipulated criteria and guidelines of the Home Possible program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Amounts specify the maximum conforming loan limits for mortgage applications, crucial in determining how much can be borrowed based on property types."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Amounts refers to the monetary limits set for loans under the FHA guidelines, varying by county and based on the property's value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Amounts refer to the minimum and maximum amounts that can be borrowed under the Advantage program, with specified limits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c4e62420861ecd803f90fd967a2c1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d10b59eabaab0b4bdac98f88233ce6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 61}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 341}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 789}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCOUNT POINTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Discount Points are fees that lenders may charge, affecting the overall cost and interest rate of the VA IRRRL loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 486}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRI-MERGE CREDIT REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Tri-Merge Credit Report is a comprehensive credit report from three bureaus required for assessing credit scores for potential borrowers in the IRRRL process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 433}]</data>
</node>
