</node>
<node id="&quot;RESOURCE FOR BORROWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Resource for Borrowers refers to the VA website and associated documents that provide eligibility and application information for the IRRRL program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VA FUNDING FEE RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The VA Funding Fee Rate is the percentage fee applied to VA loans, determined by various factors including the type of loan and borrower status."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXISTING VA LOAN BALANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Existing VA Loan Balance refers to the total amount due on an active VA loan that can be refinanced through the IRRRL program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCIPAL AND INTEREST PAYMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Principal and Interest Payments are the components of loan payments that go towards the loan balance and the interest accrued, central to the structure of VA loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELIGIBILITY GUIDELINES DOCUMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Eligibility Guidelines Document contains detailed information on which types of properties and borrowers qualify for the IRRRL program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNDERWRITING REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Underwriting Requirements refer to the standards and criteria that lenders must follow when assessing loan applications for the IRRRL program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 487}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN PROCESSING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Processing Guidelines provide instructions on how to properly process loans under the IRRRL program, including necessary documentation and steps."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 496}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 828}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Limits are the maximum amounts that can be borrowed under specific loan programs, including the guidelines set forth for HomeReady loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Limits define the maximum amounts allowed for VA loans, which vary based on the number of units and other factors, impacting IRRRL eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Limits refer to the maximum amount of mortgage that can be secured under Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac guidelines, which can vary by location and type of property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f8738c76594c2ed9866d0e86818ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 72}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT FOUNDATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Permanent Foundation is a requirement for certain types of properties, including manufactured homes, to be eligible for financing under the IRRRL program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent Foundation refers to a stable base for manufactured and modular homes, necessary for securing financing and occupancy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent foundation refers to the structural base required for certain types of manufactured homes to meet eligibility standards in financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 359}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCURATE CREDIT SCORE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Accurate Credit Score is crucial for loan qualification under the IRRRL program, reflecting a borrower's creditworthiness and repayment ability."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 87}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 433}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DIRECT TO VA REGIONAL OFFICE PROCESSING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Direct to VA Regional Office Processing refers to the requirement that certain IRRRL loans, such as those over 30 days past due, must be submitted directly to a regional VA office for approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 109}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 487}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;IRRRL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"IRRRL (Interest Rate Reduction Refinancing Loan) refers to a type of loan with a funding fee of 0.5% and specific adjustable rate details."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 102}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;5/1 ARM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"5/1 ARM is a type of adjustable-rate mortgage noted for its initial interest rate change that will occur within 60 to 66 months based on the first payment date."&lt;SEP&gt;"5/1 ARM is an adjustable rate mortgage product where the interest rate is fixed for the first five years and adjusts thereafter according to specified caps and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"5/1 ARM refers to a type of adjustable-rate mortgage with an initial fixed rate for five years and periodic adjustments thereafter."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-04a4d78a32f7dce438d7f1d06834d5ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2fe6bde08b88616e4d4932fe5f5e5c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 102}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLAGSTAR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">Flagstar is a financial institution known for its involvement in mortgage lending and providing a variety of loan products and services such as Jumbo ARMs, Doctor Loans, FHA loans, and underwriting support. They offer closing documents and services through their Web Based Closing Docs (WBCD) service and play a role in managing loan processing, evaluation, and fee disclosures. Flagstar establishes standards for conducting business in the mortgage industry, including approval processes and compliance requirements. They are involved in underwriting conforming and non-conforming loans, administering various fee structures for loan processing, and compensating brokers for originating loans, including HELOCs. Flagstar also acts as a private investor in the secondary market, buying and selling Mortgage Loans, repurchasing loans, and providing specific resources for brokers. Additionally, they have specific policies in place for loan processing, lock extensions, and managing loans during changing interest rate environments. Overall, Flagstar is a financial services organization serving real estate and financial professionals while emphasizing adherence to laws and guidelines in all transactions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b2fbf5161dc5c6670b7fd7548d822a73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6a7f245e88177bac6b85d5f808ebd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-780584b6e27004b17c25020078807812&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dcf3f3e40f27441645f474e46347d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-132b3969367ecce54c6730fb570430ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9351b24bca225d97ff2d45b46310a878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d2fd985d041d5eb6aeccbb1d21a81c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7de83587d951a7ec74fcb94d81a7df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a39b79f6d626310fd702e88ad4acda2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af318020d8f16430d1a60515a789d41d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6d8750d3b8676bc5099fb262793a7ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8254e91bb361353c2efd5fd41f17e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b42b071e6198f2a53344eeed3e0dca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717a880d45de770514dc0429a3dc79f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593f9403b246f17722c284b9fc562c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42979d97c1c73c1b28eac498c9aee682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-192e3f9f08a0121645e56ca36babd81b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f5452ea8c1afd9252c54573e518675e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94010f4bdf2ece06575cf539272b8b45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1afd5d25f6f318da0cbe2e55f0a46af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01039c48e44ce5e4ea96c87117f23d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b75506a7175a05b7c26944fe1aa93eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a48a482a40438f89f44e8758608310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fff6b81ef8a66ecc49bb49ef81869a5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f18d8da3052c73dc1f9fa6e9aef1a14e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3310e925ce8d483d790951bc5b7e818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f214a47f3746b540cbee12f81aa5bc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a4d78a32f7dce438d7f1d06834d5ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2378deca7fb18f0144fa8707001424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d10b59eabaab0b4bdac98f88233ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdba698a5ff7dd259797f2300b8f4759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1451e00f0a33296b7172a8a2f00a036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2292650099ea1cdf5881f79ed28d3cfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2fe6bde08b88616e4d4932fe5f5e5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d99ce4642f1e6e8c39678043a90b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfcbc01d9662fc8a4930eb1a9dd46384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3f42cc9266dff615db2fd5cb59e3109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc9e5323cf1da974f74cdcad0aebf55d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8552c190e01cd6c887d540f68372a1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae2131097a3957a665d280c4ed013cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f8738c76594c2ed9866d0e86818ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f639d102461efe890e188cbc182dba52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a40aeeabaca2a4a97b1dd8ad35ab142e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 79}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 394}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 799}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUERTO RICO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PUERTO RICO" is a U.S. territory located in the northeast Caribbean known for its rich cultural heritage, vibrant culture, and beautiful landscapes. It is a popular destination for Caribbean tourism. However, in the financial context, Puerto Rico has been identified as ineligible for certain mortgage and loan products, impacting borrower's access to financing options. Specifically, it is noted as not eligible for certain offerings from institutions like Flagstar Bank, Freddie Mac, and Fannie Mae. This status is due to specific eligibility restrictions and regulatory constraints placed on Puerto Rico as an unincorporated territory of the United States.&lt;SEP&gt;"Puerto Rico is a geographic location mentioned in the context of eligibility criteria for loan transactions, specifically noted as not eligible for certain refinancing options."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9cd1c976503db6a0b9762d63aba656cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0908ef3e42a9d0bcd40742960e19dbf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b42b071e6198f2a53344eeed3e0dca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91b01e6032a7e839d53d9b23f3a2949c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aade21d11a3ffb0d61652426f005667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593f9403b246f17722c284b9fc562c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eec7e8fc248456d980c970b75e0fbf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bde383f3ecde8888355124cd638e2e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11f5ef3fffef89b593ca081411d1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a4d78a32f7dce438d7f1d06834d5ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a2fe6bde08b88616e4d4932fe5f5e5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c977b52194d7751d347d7a9c63060b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72060811d2de811b03ec94848dcad94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a15606c9906902e66156e783e1ffe9b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f29d1e5fffab173b878a2ce71c0888</data>
