<node id="&quot;1-YEAR CONSTANT MATURITY TREASURY (CMT)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDEX"</data>
  <data key="d1">"1-Year CMT is a benchmark interest rate that lenders use to set loan rates that fluctuate over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"1-Year CMT is an interest rate index used to determine rates on variable loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"1-Year Constant Maturity Treasury (CMT) is an index used for determining interest rates on adjustable-rate mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"1-Year Constant Maturity Treasury (CMT) is an index used to adjust interest rates for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"1-Year Constant Maturity Treasury (CMT) is the index used for determining interest rates on adjustable-rate products."&lt;SEP&gt;"1-Year CMT is an index used in the calculation of interest rates for certain adjustable-rate mortgages, reflecting the yields of U.S. Treasury securities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bde383f3ecde8888355124cd638e2e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3310e925ce8d483d790951bc5b7e818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8760dceb193fd7c5f24d24209ee5e31</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 102}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 460}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 813}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEGATIVE AMORTIZATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Negative Amortization is a concept referring to a loan condition where the loan balance increases due to payments not covering the interest charged."&lt;SEP&gt;"Negative Amortization is a situation where the loan balance increases over time due to payments that do not cover interest costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Negative Amortization refers to a situation in which the loan balance increases due to deferred interest payments that exceed the actual payments made."&lt;SEP&gt;"Negative Amortization is a loan feature where the monthly payments are less than the interest due, causing the loan balance to increase over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Negative Amortization occurs when the payments on a loan are not sufficient to cover the interest due, leading to an increase in the loan balance over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Negative Amortization occurs when monthly payments are less than the interest charged, causing the loan balance to increase over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Negative Amortization occurs when the payments made are not sufficient to cover the interest, resulting in an increase in the principal balance of the loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Negative Amortization occurs when the payments made on a loan are less than the accrued interest, causing the loan balance to increase over time."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6a2fe6bde08b88616e4d4932fe5f5e5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3310e925ce8d483d790951bc5b7e818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eec7e8fc248456d980c970b75e0fbf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f8738c76594c2ed9866d0e86818ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11f5ef3fffef89b593ca081411d1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6d8750d3b8676bc5099fb262793a7ff</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 108}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 480}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEREST RATE ADJUSTMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest Rate Adjustment pertains to the periodic changes in interest rates for loans such as the 5/1 ARM, occurring every 12 months after the initial period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Rate Adjustment refers to the periodic changes in the interest rate on an adjustable-rate mortgage based on a specified index."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Rate Adjustment refers to the regular updates of loan interest rates as specified in the documentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f11f5ef3fffef89b593ca081411d1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a4d78a32f7dce438d7f1d06834d5ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 102}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 462}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLOSING DOCS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Closing Docs are necessary documentation ordered through Flagstar's WBCD service, which facilitates the closing of loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Docs are the documentation required to finalize a mortgage transaction, encompassing all necessary forms and agreements needed for closing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Docs refer to the necessary documents that finalize a mortgage transaction, ensuring all parties understand their rights and obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Docs refer to documentation required at the end of a loan process to finalize the mortgage transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Docs refer to the legal documents required to finalize a mortgage or loan transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Docs refers to documentation processes used during the mortgage closing process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Docs are the final set of documents that must be signed by the parties involved in a real estate transaction to finalize the mortgage and transfer of ownership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Docs refers to the documentation required to finalize a real estate transaction, ensuring compliance and proper record-keeping."&lt;SEP&gt;"Closing Docs refers to the documentation and processes involved in finalizing mortgage agreements and transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a72060811d2de811b03ec94848dcad94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593f9403b246f17722c284b9fc562c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bde383f3ecde8888355124cd638e2e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11f5ef3fffef89b593ca081411d1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6d8750d3b8676bc5099fb262793a7ff</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 114}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 509}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATE ELIGIBILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"STATE ELIGIBILITY outlines the specific states and territories where the Fannie Mae HomeReady product can be accessed, along with their respective restrictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"State Eligibility denotes the conditions under which mortgage products can be accessed based on geographic locations."&lt;SEP&gt;"State Eligibility encompasses the conditions under which specific mortgage products can be offered based on geographic criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"State Eligibility encompasses the regulations determining which states can participate in specific loan or insurance programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"State Eligibility refers to the criteria determining the availability of certain mortgage products based on geographical restrictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"State Eligibility refers to the list and restrictions of states where certain mortgage products are available."&lt;SEP&gt;"State Eligibility refers to the criteria determining which states are eligible for specific loan products and the associated restrictions."&lt;SEP&gt;"State Eligibility refers to the geographic restrictions and availability of FHA programs in specific states."</data>
