<node id="&quot;ADJUSTMENT CAPS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Adjustment Caps are limits on how much the interest rate can increase during adjustment periods in adjustable-rate mortgages, protecting borrowers from excessive rate hikes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustment Caps are limits on how much the interest rate on a loan can change during adjustment periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustment Caps are limits placed on how much the interest rate on a loan can adjust during each adjustment period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustment Caps are provisions that limit how much the interest rate on a mortgage can change during an adjustment period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustment Caps refer to the limits on how much the interest rate can increase or decrease during specific adjustment periods for adjustable-rate mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustment Caps set limits on how much interest rates can change during each adjustment period for adjustable-rate mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustment Caps are limits placed on how much interest rates can change with each adjustment period for variable rate loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustment Caps are restrictions on how much an interest rate can change over time, relevant in the context of financial product guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustment Caps refer to limits on how much the interest rate can change during each adjustment period for financial products like HELOCs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Adjustment Caps refer to the limits on how much interest rates can change over time in adjustable-rate mortgage products, indicating a financial mechanism to protect borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9cd1c976503db6a0b9762d63aba656cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b42b071e6198f2a53344eeed3e0dca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3310e925ce8d483d790951bc5b7e818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72060811d2de811b03ec94848dcad94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eec7e8fc248456d980c970b75e0fbf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bde383f3ecde8888355124cd638e2e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 103}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 466}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARGIN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Margin indicates the percentage added to the index rate, determining the overall interest rate on loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Margin is a term used to determine the interest rate for HELOCs based on the borrower's credit profiles and market conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Margin is the additional amount added to the index value to determine the interest rate for adjustable-rate loans, noted in the price indication sheet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Margin refers to the difference between the index value and the interest rate set by the lender, affecting adjustable-rate mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Margin is the fixed difference added to an index rate that determines a borrower's new interest rate after adjustments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Margin is the fixed percentage added to an index rate to calculate the interest rate on an adjustable-rate mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Margin is the fixed percentage added to the index to determine the interest rate on an adjustable-rate mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Margin refers to the fixed percentage added to the index rate to determine the interest rate for adjustable-rate loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Margin refers to the difference between the interest rate of a loan and the index rate, determining the overall cost of the loan for borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Margin is the percentage added to the index value to determine the interest rate for variable rate loans, affecting the borrower's payment amounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Margin refers to the difference added to the index rate that determines the interest rate for financial products, such as HELOCs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9cd1c976503db6a0b9762d63aba656cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c977b52194d7751d347d7a9c63060b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72060811d2de811b03ec94848dcad94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eec7e8fc248456d980c970b75e0fbf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bde383f3ecde8888355124cd638e2e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11f5ef3fffef89b593ca081411d1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 102}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 460}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 814}]</data>
</node>
