  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Change Dates are specific dates on which interest rates on adjustable-rate loans are subject to change, crucial for borrowers to track."&lt;SEP&gt;"Change Dates are specific points in time outlined in loan documentation when interest rates adjust for products like the 5/1 ARM."&lt;SEP&gt;"Change Dates refer to specific points in time when the interest rate on an adjustable-rate mortgage may be adjusted based on the terms of the loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Change Dates are specific points in time when the interest rate on an adjustable-rate mortgage is adjusted, affecting the borrower's payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Change Dates refer to specific dates on which interest rates may be adjusted based on the terms of the loan agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Change Dates refer to specific times when the interest rate adjusts in adjustable-rate mortgage products, affecting payment amounts."</data>
