</node>
<node id="&quot;HIGH BALANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"High Balance refers to a category of loans that exceed certain limits for high-cost areas and are eligible under specific products like HomeStyle."&lt;SEP&gt;"High Balance refers to a type of loan product that exceeds the conforming loan limits established by the Federal Housing Finance Agency."&lt;SEP&gt;"High Balance refers to the mortgages offered under the HomeReady-HomeStyle program that exceed conventional loan limits, available in various fixed-rate terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"High Balance refers to loan amounts that exceed conforming loan limits and are subjected to higher requirements based on the county's cost standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f626d237ebaf21492fcd8cbd9a81536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c4e62420861ecd803f90fd967a2c1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27bd5ad2c70145086339257520820a41</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 786}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENOVATION PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROGRAM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Renovation Program allows borrowers to merge the purchase or refinance of a home with renovation costs, ensuring funds are properly managed and allocated post-renovation completion."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LTV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LTV, or Loan-To-Value, is a financial term used to describe the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, presented for various loan types in the comparison."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV, or Loan-to-Value Ratio, is a financial ratio that compares the loan amount to the appraised value of a property."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV, or Loan-to-Value, is a financial term used to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, used in determining cash out options."&lt;SEP&gt;LTV (Loan-to-Value) is a financial term used by lenders to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased. It plays a significant role in mortgage terms and eligibility, impacting borrowing limits, loan conditions, and the approval process. LTV, or Loan-To-Value ratio, is crucial for determining mortgage terms, assessing loan eligibility, and evaluating the ratio of the loan amount to the appraised value of the property. This ratio is essential in various lending situations, including mortgage lending and refinancing. Additionally, LTV is a critical measure used in HomeReady eligibility, influencing loan terms based on property value and equity.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6de80860713bbcd40afb3b3b69d1945f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d2fd985d041d5eb6aeccbb1d21a81c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bc9ce80658e51e7fed2cac493270e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad5bfdaee64eed200866a097fc789e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b75506a7175a05b7c26944fe1aa93eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12641cd1a4c93cf93c1aa31082da47b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a582fe17fe66be19c89056580dbaccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd698c420bb978f364630c455d2abf4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3f42cc9266dff615db2fd5cb59e3109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc754fc30ff722a8fee09393323a03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a577e8766cf4f0e1ae599795cd9c6fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f29d1e5fffab173b878a2ce71c0888&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c57c1331aa9873de4467468c1b07505</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT SCORE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "Credit Score" is a numerical representation of a borrower's creditworthiness, derived from a level analysis of credit files. It is a critical factor in determining loan approval, terms, and interest rates for various mortgage programs such as Home Possible, HomeReady, HELOCs, and Advantage program. Lenders use the credit score to evaluate the likelihood of a borrower repaying their debts and to assess financial reliability, influencing eligibility for loans under different conditions and programs.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bc9ce80658e51e7fed2cac493270e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad5bfdaee64eed200866a097fc789e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3310e925ce8d483d790951bc5b7e818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df57131d49eba22a5ca15cafeb404cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f28aa24c80be0008755d728b5169b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a582fe17fe66be19c89056580dbaccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfcbc01d9662fc8a4930eb1a9dd46384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3f42cc9266dff615db2fd5cb59e3109</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 330}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 787}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ESCROW ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Escrow Account is a financial arrangement where funds are held by a third party on behalf of the borrower to pay property taxes and insurance."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Escrow Account is a financial tool used to hold funds for future payments, in this context used for managing renovation funds until work completion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow Account is a neutral account where funds are held by a third party before a transaction is completed, often used for handling transaction funds in real estate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow Account is a financial arrangement where funds are held by a third party until certain conditions are met, commonly used in real estate transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow Account is a third-party account where funds are held on behalf of the borrower for taxes and insurance, although not allowed for HELOCs as per guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow Account is a financial arrangement that allows a third party to hold funds on behalf of the borrower and lender during the mortgage process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow Account is a financial arrangement where funds are held by a third party on behalf of the borrowers and lenders until the loan conditions are fulfilled, important in mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow Account is a special account where funds are held by a third party on behalf of the buyer and lender, often used for property taxes and insurance."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-283d5323d92a66b703dacfb0b3c98a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aade21d11a3ffb0d61652426f005667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de34030d71ef2c627010a089db20697c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3f42cc9266dff615db2fd5cb59e3109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eec7e8fc248456d980c970b75e0fbf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a577e8766cf4f0e1ae599795cd9c6fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 43}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 286}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WARRANTABLE CONDO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Warrantable Condo is a condominium that meets certain requirements set by lenders, making it eligible for financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condo is a type of condominium that meets specific criteria for financing and insurance purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condo is a type of property commonly used in mortgage applications with specific guidelines for loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condo is a type of property eligible under the HomeReady-HomeStyle program for financing, meeting specific criteria for buyers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condo refers to a type of condominium that meets certain eligibility criteria for financing under Fannie Mae guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condo refers to a condominium that meets the eligibility requirements for mortgage financing under Freddie Mac's guidelines, allowing for conventional financing options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condos are a type of condominium that meets lender guidelines, allowing for their financing under specific mortgage programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condo is a type of condominium that meets the requirements set out to qualify for the Home Possible mortgage program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condos are condominium units that meet certain criteria making them eligible for financing under Home Possible."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condo refers to a condominium that meets certain criteria set by lenders, making it eligible for financing and resale."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condo signifies a classification for condominiums that meet certain lending guidelines, allowing them to be financed through conventional loan programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condo is a type of property mentioned as eligible for the Home Equity Line of Credit"&lt;SEP&gt;"Warrantable Condo refers to condominiums that meet eligibility requirements set by Fannie Mae, allowing them to be financed through the HomeReady program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-304d9428ac3f0546fe2c83618fb493e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc754fc30ff722a8fee09393323a03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad5bfdaee64eed200866a097fc789e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a582fe17fe66be19c89056580dbaccc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 328}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PUD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A PUD, or Planned Unit Development, is a type of property development that allows for a mix of residential and commercial properties, also mentioned as an eligible housing type under the HomeReady program."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUD refers to Planned Unit Developments, which are properties eligible for the Home Equity Line of Credit."&lt;SEP&gt;PUD, which stands for Planned Unit Development, refers to a specific type of property ownership structure often used in real estate transactions. It denotes a residential community designed as a single entity with shared amenities and recreational spaces, where units may share common areas and amenities, affecting loan criteria and approvals. These communities can consist of grouped homes, possibly combined with commercial properties, and are eligible for financing under various programs such as HomeReady-HomeStyle, Home Possible loans, and construction loans. PUDs are characterized by a mix of residential homes and commercial properties, with shared amenities, recognized under lending guidelines and mortgage eligibility criteria. This type of property includes common areas and amenities shared among residents, allowing for mixed-use communities with various housing types and amenities, and a cohesive community layout.&lt;SEP&gt;"PUD stands for Planned Unit Development, a type of housing development that includes residential and commercial components, managed by a homeowners association."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUD, or Planned Unit Development, is a type of property eligible for FHA loans, which may include a mix of residential and commercial units."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUD refers to Planned Unit Development, a housing development that blends residential, commercial, and public space, offering unique financial and property management criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"PUD refers to Planned Unit Development, a type of real estate development that includes residential housing and uses within a defined area."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6de80860713bbcd40afb3b3b69d1945f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304d9428ac3f0546fe2c83618fb493e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad5bfdaee64eed200866a097fc789e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a582fe17fe66be19c89056580dbaccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27bd5ad2c70145086339257520820a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc754fc30ff722a8fee09393323a03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-060d3305d5697520404f94c4fcd2cb85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 328}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;2-UNIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"2-Unit describes a property type with two units that qualifies for the Home Possible mortgage products under specified terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"2-Unit is a classification of properties eligible for financing under the HomeReady-HomeStyle program, indicating duplex structures that can be financed."&lt;SEP&gt;"2-Unit refers to a residential property that contains two separate living units, which can be financed under specific mortgage guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"2-Unit refers to a property classification indicating that the mortgage applies to a duplex, allowing for financing on buildings with two distinct living units."&lt;SEP&gt;"2-Unit refers to properties that contain two separated housing units, relevant for determining eligibility in financing options."&lt;SEP&gt;"2-Unit identifies properties designed for two separate living units, qualifying for certain mortgage offerings intended for multi-family residences."&lt;SEP&gt;"2-Unit refers to a two-family home that qualifies for mortgage products mentioned in the document, allowing for the financing of multi-family residences."&lt;SEP&gt;"2-Unit refers to duplex properties that are eligible for financing under the HomeReady loan program with specific LTV limits."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a582fe17fe66be19c89056580dbaccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 785}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;3 TO 4-UNIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"3 to 4-Unit describes properties that have three or four separate housing units, also important for loan eligibility criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"3 to 4-Unit properties indicate multi-family residential buildings with up to four units that are eligible for the Home Possible program."&lt;SEP&gt;"3 to 4-Unit refers to a property classification indicating that the mortgage applies to multi-family buildings with three to four distinct living units."&lt;SEP&gt;"3 to 4-Unit refers to multi-family properties that contain three to four individual rental units, which are subject to distinct financing rules."&lt;SEP&gt;"3 to 4-Unit refers to properties with three or four units that are eligible for financing under the HomeReady-HomeStyle program, allowing for multi-family financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"3 to 4-Unit refers to multi-family properties containing three to four units that can be financed under specified guidelines for HomeReady loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a582fe17fe66be19c89056580dbaccc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 327}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 785}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DU&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DU is a software platform used by lenders to assess risk and provide underwriting recommendations regarding mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU, or Desktop Underwriter, is a technology platform used to evaluate loan applications for eligibility and risk assessment in the mortgage industry."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU, or Desktop Underwriter, is an automated underwriting system used to assess mortgage eligibility and streamline the loan approval process."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU stands for Desktop Underwriter, an automated underwriting tool provided by Fannie Mae used to assess mortgage loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU, or Desktop Underwriter, is an automated underwriting system used to assess mortgage eligibility and risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU refers to an organization involved in the approval process for financing, perhaps representing a university or institution."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU stands for Desktop Underwriter, a computer program used by mortgage lenders to assess the eligibility of a loan application."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU is an organization involved in the loan application process, using cash-on-hand to assess available funds for closing."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU, or Desktop Underwriter, is an automated underwriting system used by lenders to assess eligibility for Fannie Mae's loan products, including HomeReady."&lt;SEP&gt;"DU stands for Desktop Underwriter, a technology utilized by lenders to automate the underwriting process for mortgage applications and assess related risks."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92bc9ce80658e51e7fed2cac493270e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc754fc30ff722a8fee09393323a03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2b0ee234c74087767f8bbd0d6c44e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad5bfdaee64eed200866a097fc789e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 182}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEREST EARNING ACCOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Interest Earning Account is a type of savings account that earns interest on the balance, relevant for managing renovation funds in the HomeReady-HomeStyle program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SOFT COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Soft Costs refer to expenses associated with a real estate project that are not direct construction costs, which in this case can be financed under the renovation program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soft Costs refer to expenses related to construction projects like architectural, engineering, and permit fees that may be financed under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soft Costs refer to the non-tangible expenses incurred in the construction process, such as permits and engineering fees, that can be financed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71f642eb6cc44e3fc724fd1b5beeccd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-060d3305d5697520404f94c4fcd2cb85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDER THIRD-PARTY CONTRACTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Builder Third-Party Contracts are agreements between borrowers and licensed builders that are necessary for funding renovation projects under the HomeReady-HomeStyle program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN REGISTRATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Registration involves entering the details of a down payment assistance loan into a system such as Loantrac, to ensure proper tracking and compliance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Registration is a procedure involving the selection of product options necessary for completing the mortgage application process with Fannie Mae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Registration outlines the process of registering for different types of loans and the relevant conditions associated with them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Registration is the process of formally entering loan information into a system to confirm it is eligible for specific programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Registration is an event that involves registering loan details and purposes for construction financing, ensuring compliance with required protocols."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Registration refers to the administrative process of entering loan details into a system to facilitate the approval and management of loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Registration is the process of formally documenting a mortgage application and its associated details in the lending system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Registration is the process of formally entering a loan into a system, assigning it a loan number, and establishing its terms and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Registration is the process whereby a correspondent registers a loan with Flagstar Bank, adhering to specific procedures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Registration refers to the process of officially enrolling a loan application and collecting necessary information from the borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Registration refers to the process of registering loans with a financial institution, including specific procedures and guidelines for brokers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8c6c6dd97681ba9caa6c83d8ddf9ec59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77f9a0c774af974e032ea5bf1841d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27bd5ad2c70145086339257520820a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c4e62420861ecd803f90fd967a2c1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1afd5d25f6f318da0cbe2e55f0a46af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 126}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 536}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income Limits are defined thresholds regarding borrower eligibility for particular loan products, particularly in affordable lending contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income Limits refer to the criteria set for income levels that determine eligibility for the HomeReady-HomeStyle program, ensuring it serves low to moderate income borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income Limits pertain to the maximum income thresholds that borrowers must adhere to qualify for the HomeReady loan program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income Limits refer to the maximum income levels that borrowers must adhere to in order to qualify for specific housing loans, particularly aimed at affordable housing initiatives."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c4e62420861ecd803f90fd967a2c1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 373}]</data>
</node>
