<node id="&quot;MAXIMUM LTV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maximum LTV (Loan-To-Value) is the highest ratio of the loan amount to the appraised value of the property, affecting what is available for borrowing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV or maximum loan-to-value is the highest percentage of the property value that can be financed through a loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV refers to the highest loan-to-value ratio allowed for securing a mortgage, indicating how much can be borrowed against an asset's value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV refers to the maximum loan-to-value ratio permitted under the HomeReady-HomeStyle program, which allows for higher financing on certain properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV, or Loan-To-Value ratio, is a financial term indicating the highest percentage of the home's value that can be borrowed, crucial for determining loan eligibility and amounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV (Loan-to-Value) is a financial term used to express the ratio of a loan to the value of the property purchased, crucial for lending decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV indicates the highest loan-to-value ratio acceptable by lenders for various types of property purchases or refinances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV refers to the highest loan-to-value ratio that can be permitted for various types of construction loans, indicating lending risk and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV is the highest loan-to-value ratio that lenders will accept for a mortgage, a key factor in determining lending risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV (Loan-to-Value) is the highest permissible ratio of the loan amount compared to the appraised value of the property, crucial for qualifying for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV, or Loan-to-Value ratio, represents a mathematical figure indicating the maximum amount of a loan compared to the appraised value of the property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV stands for Maximum Loan-to-Value Ratio, indicating the maximum ratio of a loan to the value of the asset purchased."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV (Loan-to-Value) indicates the highest ratio of a loan amount compared to the appraised value of the property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum LTV (Loan-to-Value) is a financial measurement used to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, affecting mortgage approval terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92bc9ce80658e51e7fed2cac493270e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0bf252dda6ffda0104c759447cefbb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e49ff67fbaa2b705ebcac9802c0c64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-060d3305d5697520404f94c4fcd2cb85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a582fe17fe66be19c89056580dbaccc</data>
