  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maximum CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) and HCLTV (High Combined Loan-to-Value) refers to the upper limits for these ratios when calculating loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) and HCLTV (Home Combined Loan-to-Value) represent ratios for loans that include multiple liens against the same property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum CLTV/HCLTV refers to the maximum combined loan-to-value ratios that can be utilized in financing, crucial for assessing borrowing limits under the HomeReady-HomeStyle program."</data>
