<node id="&quot;LTV, CLTV, HCLTV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LTV (Loan-to-Value), CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value), and HCLTV (High Combined Loan-to-Value) are financial metrics used to assess the risk level of a loan relative to the value of the property."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV (Loan-to-Value), CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value), and HCLTV (Home Equity Combined Loan-to-Value) are ratios used to assess the borrower's equity in their property relative to the loans secured against it."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c4e62420861ecd803f90fd967a2c1c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 372}]</data>
</node>
