</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH-OUT REFINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CASH-OUT REFINANCE is a financial transaction where the borrower refinances their home for more than they owe, taking the difference in cash, and is mentioned as a loan type connected to the Home Equity Line of Credit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out refinance is a type of transaction allowed under HELOC strategies, enabling borrowers to access equity while refinancing their current mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;CASH-OUT REFINANCE is a financial strategy or event where homeowners refinance their existing mortgage for an amount greater than what they owe, allowing them to access the equity in their property in cash. This process involves taking on additional loan responsibilities and can be used to consolidate debt, fund renovations, or integrate the new loan into the homeowner's financial strategy. The transaction is structured according to specific standards, such as VA guidelines, and involves borrowers accessing cash based on their property's equity. Ultimately, CASH-OUT REFINANCE enables borrowers to unlock the equity in their home for various financial needs.&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a refinancing option that enables homeowners to take cash out from their equity while obtaining a new mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a type of refinancing that allows homeowners to take out a new mortgage for more than they owe on their existing mortgage and receive the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"CASH-OUT REFINANCE is a type of financial transaction that allows homeowners to refinance their mortgage and receive cash from the equity of their home."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a mortgage refinancing option allowing homeowners to borrow against their home's equity, receiving the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a type of refinancing option that allows Borrowers to take out a loan larger than the existing mortgage to access cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a type of refinancing option that allows borrowers to take out a loan larger than the existing mortgage to access cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-Out Refinance is a loan option that allows homeowners to take out a new mortgage for more than they owe on their existing mortgage, using the difference to access cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash-out Refinance is a mortgage refinancing option where the homeowner takes out a new mortgage for more than the amount owed and receives the difference in cash."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8760dceb193fd7c5f24d24209ee5e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b42b071e6198f2a53344eeed3e0dca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b06bf2c39f8da79b3399842638c80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bc9ce80658e51e7fed2cac493270e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4c4e62420861ecd803f90fd967a2c1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42979d97c1c73c1b28eac498c9aee682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94010f4bdf2ece06575cf539272b8b45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad5bfdaee64eed200866a097fc789e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01039c48e44ce5e4ea96c87117f23d78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c57c1331aa9873de4467468c1b07505</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 315}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 782}]</data>
</node>
