<node id="&quot;MODULAR HOMES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Modular Homes are prefabricated homes that are built in sections and then assembled on-site, meeting specific building standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Modular Homes are properties constructed in sections off-site, which take on the characteristics of site-built homes when installed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Modular Homes are prefabricated structures that are manufactured off-site and assembled at the final location, generally eligible for loans under certain conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Modular homes are prefabricated structures built in sections and can be transported and assembled on-site."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f28aa24c80be0008755d728b5169b82</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 359}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PLANNED UNIT DEVELOPMENT (PUD)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Planned Unit Development (PUD) is a community development that includes residential and commercial properties, each with its own financial and eligibility requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planned Unit Development (PUD) is a type of property ownership that includes specific requirements for mortgage policies, emphasizing the need for ALTA endorsements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planned Unit Development (PUD) refers to a type of real estate development that is eligible under the guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planned Unit Development (PUD) refers to a type of residential community that is planned and developed as a single entity and allows for a mix of uses including residential and sometimes commercial."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planned Unit Developments (PUDs) are communities that maintain shared facilities and common areas, qualifying for financing under certain mortgage programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planned Unit Development (PUD) refers to a type of building development and regulations that allows for mixed-use and planned community layouts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planned Unit Development (PUD) is a type of community development that includes residential and commercial spaces and is often subject to specific zoning regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Planned Unit Development (PUD) is recognized as an eligible property type for FHA financing, which may include various housing arrangements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Planned Unit Development (PUD) refers to a community where residential units are part of an overall development ensuring planned amenities and facilities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0bf252dda6ffda0104c759447cefbb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25dcfc163b5b00ffab734b755ea03592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f28aa24c80be0008755d728b5169b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d10b59eabaab0b4bdac98f88233ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e572c9b9bd53e500c5e02283f3230e6b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 362}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONVENTIONAL UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines are a set of criteria used by lenders to evaluate the risk associated with providing mortgage loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines are standards set forth for underwriting conventional mortgage loans to assess borrower eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines are the established set of rules and criteria determined by Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac for evaluating mortgage loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines are the standards and practices that lenders use to assess the creditworthiness of borrowers and the risks associated with mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines consist of the criteria and standards used to evaluate mortgage applications for conventional loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines refer to the protocols and standards used to assess the creditworthiness of borrowers applying for conventional loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines offer criteria for lending processes associated with conventional mortgages, ensuring compliance with established standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines refer to the rules and requirements in the mortgage industry that govern how loans are processed and approved."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines refer to the set of standards and rules used to evaluate and approve mortgage loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines are referenced as the document that outlines the requirements and criteria for mortgage loans and refinancing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines are the standards set by financial institutions, like Freddie Mac, for processing mortgage loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines refer to the set of standards that govern mortgage loan qualifications and approval processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Conventional Underwriting Guidelines outline the standards and requirements that must be met for loan approvals in conventional financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines refer to the standardized rules used by lenders to evaluate mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Conventional Underwriting Guidelines outline the criteria and requirements for loan processing and approvals in the mortgage industry, including HomeReady loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Conventional Underwriting Guidelines are standards set for evaluating mortgage applications and loan risk taken by Flagstar Bank."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Conventional Underwriting Guidelines provide standards and rules for underwriting conventional loans, ensuring compliance with established lending practices."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Conventional Underwriting Guidelines are procedures that dictate the requirements for closing loans in a trust, ensuring compliance with regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines are the set of rules governing the underwriting process for conventional loans issued by Flagstar."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conventional Underwriting Guidelines refer to the set of standards and procedures that govern the assessment and approval of conventional loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe4b9e8302b8de2d8d692106e4e284ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2d9f6b5b471373ca78f75c11d02725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6a7f245e88177bac6b85d5f808ebd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a403e885ce18327dd600e7521b66a2e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662a2c10d200da7291e0212d33749544&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f5452ea8c1afd9252c54573e518675e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1418f5447a956615e29938e7c6f0f71a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a675c08f3177636cb84734aead2aea</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 579}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DESKTOP UNDERWRITER (DU)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Desktop Underwriter (DU) is a software used for determining loan eligibility based on provided criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Desktop Underwriter (DU) is an automated underwriting system provided by Fannie Mae to evaluate the credit risk of mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Desktop Underwriter (DU) is an automated underwriting system used by lenders to evaluate a borrower's eligibility for a mortgage, incorporating various financial criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Desktop Underwriter (DU) is an automated underwriting tool used to assess loan applications and determine eligibility for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Desktop Underwriter (DU) is an automated underwriting system used by lenders to evaluate mortgage applications and determine borrower eligibility for loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25dcfc163b5b00ffab734b755ea03592</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 335}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTINGENCY RESERVE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contingency Reserve is an amount set aside within a renovation budget to cover unforeseen expenses that may arise during a renovation project."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 159}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRINCIPAL RESIDENCE PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Principal Residence Property refers to the primary home that a borrower occupies, which is subject to renovation and financing options."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME-ELIGIBLE OCCUPANT BORROWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income-Eligible Occupant Borrowers are individuals who qualify for mortgage financing based on their income and occupancy status of the property being financed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income-eligible occupant borrowers are individuals whose income qualifies them for loans under the Home Possible program, typically linked to community lending efforts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 571}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECURITIZED LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Securitized Loans are loans that have been pooled together and sold as securities to investors, often indicating mortgage-backed securities."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENOVATION DRAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renovation Draws refer to the funds disbursed for renovation projects during the course of a loan, based on the completion of certain milestones."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 159}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Eligibility Criteria are the requirements that must be met to qualify for a particular mortgage product."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Criteria encompass the specific conditions that properties and borrowers must meet to qualify for various loan programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Criteria refer to the specific requirements that borrowers must meet to qualify for the Fannie Mae HomeReady-HomeStyle loan program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Criteria outline the specific conditions that must be met for a loan to qualify for the Hybrid eClose process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Criteria refer to the specific conditions and qualifications that must be met by applicants to access down payment assistance programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Criteria represent the standards and requirements that must be met for participation in specific loan programs or assistance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility criteria refer to the specific requirements that borrowers and properties must meet to qualify for FHA loans and insurance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Criteria are the requirements that need to be met for a Borrower to qualify for a loan, influencing approvals and refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b42b071e6198f2a53344eeed3e0dca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b722d926669aa7676c36ecbb75a4a233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27bd5ad2c70145086339257520820a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea9eec682fb4dbe92270f8b8c48a9354&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12641cd1a4c93cf93c1aa31082da47b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 136}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 571}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-OCCUPANT CO-BORROWERS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-Occupant Co-Borrowers are individuals who co-sign a mortgage loan but do not reside at the property being financed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-occupant Co-borrowers are individuals who co-sign a loan but do not live in the property being financed, which makes them ineligible in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-occupant Co-borrowers are individuals who assist applicants in getting a loan but do not live in the property, influencing loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-occupant co-borrowers can participate in HELOC applications, showing flexibility in borrower eligibility under specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-occupant co-borrowers are individuals who co-sign on a loan without living in the property, subject to specific lending guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1418f5447a956615e29938e7c6f0f71a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 127}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 543}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIXED-RATE LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Fixed-Rate Loans are mortgage loans with an interest rate that remains constant throughout the term of the loan, providing predictable monthly payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fixed-rate Loans are financial products where the interest rate remains constant throughout the loan term, providing predictable monthly payments for borrowers."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 371}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TITLE UPDATE FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Title Update Fees are charges incurred to update the title of a property during a refinancing or purchase process, ensuring clear ownership."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ARCHITECTURAL FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Architectural Fees are costs associated with hiring an architect for design and planning during renovation projects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Architectural Fees represent costs associated with hiring architects for design and planning in the construction project, eligible for financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-060d3305d5697520404f94c4fcd2cb85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENGINEERING FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Engineering Fees are expenses related to engineering services required for construction projects, which can be included in the financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Engineering Fees refer to charges for professional engineering services required for assessing and planning structural changes in a property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-060d3305d5697520404f94c4fcd2cb85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMIT FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permit Fees are costs related to obtaining legal permission from local authorities to commence renovation projects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permit Fees encompass costs to secure necessary legal permissions for construction activities, which may also be financed within the loan program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-060d3305d5697520404f94c4fcd2cb85</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 160}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ENERGY REPORT FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Energy Report Fees are charges associated with assessments of a property's energy efficiency, which may be required for certain financing programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVIEW OF RENOVATION PLANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Review of Renovation Plans refers to the process of evaluating proposed changes to a property to ensure they meet regulatory and safety standards."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONSTRUCTION AND RENOVATION GUIDE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Construction and Renovation Guide is a document that outlines the processes, requirements, and standards for carrying out construction and renovation under specific loan programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SWIMMING POOLS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Swimming Pools are outdoor water structures that may be added as part of home improvements under the HomeStyle Renovation loan program, subject to local regulations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCESSORY UNITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Accessory Units are secondary living spaces on residential properties, such as granny flats or in-law suites, that may be added through renovation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3d24b1a560ceedfac130cd557ad5adc3</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 156}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CENSUS TRACT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Census Tract is a geographic region defined for statistical purposes, used in mortgage eligibility assessments, particularly concerning income limits and FIPS codes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Census Tract refers to geographic areas used in the United States for statistical purposes, which are essential for determining income limits related to mortgage eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Census tract refers to a small, relatively permanent statistical subdivision of a county used by the U.S. Census Bureau for collecting and analyzing demographic data."&lt;SEP&gt;"Census tract refers to a geographical region defined for statistical purposes that is critical for evaluating loan eligibility and borrower contributions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AMI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AMI stands for Area Median Income, which is used to assess income eligibility for mortgage products and is essential for calculating limits in the HomeReady program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNDERWRITING GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"GUIDELINE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Underwriting Guidelines consist of the protocols and standards used by underwriters to evaluate loan applications accurately for compliance and risk assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Guidelines contain the standards and procedures used by lenders to assess the risks of lending to a borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Guidelines refer to the criteria used for reviewing mortgage applications and insurance endorsements, ensuring they meet required standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Guidelines refer to the set of policies and criteria that lenders must follow to evaluate the creditworthiness of borrowers applying for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Guidelines refer to the criteria lenders use to evaluate applicants for loans, ensuring they meet necessary standards for approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Guidelines refer to the rules and criteria lenders follow to evaluate mortgage applications and the suitability of borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Guidelines refer to the set of criteria used by lenders to determine the risk of lending money to borrowers, ensuring careful evaluation of applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Guidelines refer to the specific criteria and standards that lenders follow when assessing loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ca3069902295dcf5b2b505753d7623f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aade21d11a3ffb0d61652426f005667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12641cd1a4c93cf93c1aa31082da47b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e572c9b9bd53e500c5e02283f3230e6b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 116}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 517}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HOMEOWNERSHIP EDUCATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Homeownership Education is a prerequisite course aimed at educating first-time homebuyers about the mortgage process and responsibilities associated with homeownership."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeownership Education is a program area that entails guiding potential homeowners through the process of buying a home and managing a mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeownership Education is an event that requires first-time homebuyers to complete a course to become eligible for certain mortgage loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeownership Education refers to programs designed to inform potential homeowners about financing, responsibilities, and the home buying process required for loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeownership Education is a program designed to equip potential home buyers with knowledge and guidance on the home purchasing process, often required for certain mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeownership Education refers to programs and courses that first-time homebuyers must complete to understand the responsibilities and processes involved in owning a home."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd698c420bb978f364630c455d2abf4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a403e885ce18327dd600e7521b66a2e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 374}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME ELIGIBILITY LOOKUP TOOL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TOOL"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income Eligibility Lookup Tool is an online resource provided by Fannie Mae to assist borrowers in determining their eligibility for financing based on income limits."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Income Eligibility Lookup Tool is a technology tool on the Fannie Mae website that allows potential borrowers to determine their eligibility based on income and location."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 373}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIPS CODE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"FIPS Code is a standardized code used to identify regions in the United States, essential for confirming income limits in housing finance."&lt;SEP&gt;"FIPS Code is a standardized numerical code used to identify geographic regions for data collection and income limit determination in mortgage loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 373}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER PERSONAL FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower Personal Funds are the financial resources that come directly from the borrower's savings or investment accounts, typically used for down payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrower Personal Funds refers to the financial resources that are contributed by borrowers from their own savings, which are required to qualify for financing under the HomeReady program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrower Personal Funds refer to the funds that a borrower supplies from their own resources as part of the down payment or contribution for mortgage loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a403e885ce18327dd600e7521b66a2e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 198}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 710}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FRAMEWORK HOMEOWNERSHIP EDUCATION COURSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROGRAM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Framework Homeownership Education Course is a required educational program that first-time homebuyers must complete to qualify for specific mortgage loans under the HomeReady program."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Framework Homeownership Education course is an educational program designed for aspiring homebuyers, particularly first-time buyers, to learn about the home purchasing process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 374}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANUAL UNDERWRITING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Manual Underwriting involves the evaluation of a borrower's application and financial situation by a human underwriter, as opposed to automated systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manual Underwriting is the process where a human underwriter evaluates a mortgage application and its associated risks rather than utilizing automated systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manual Underwriting is the process where a loan application is evaluated by a human underwriter when automated systems cannot approve it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Manual Underwriting refers to the traditional method of evaluating a borrower's ability to repay a loan, often used when standard automated processes are not suitable."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1b06bf2c39f8da79b3399842638c80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3069902295dcf5b2b505753d7623f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 188}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-TRADITIONAL CREDIT PROFILES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-Traditional Credit Profiles are credit assessments used to evaluate borrowers who may not have conventional credit histories, making them eligible for specialized loan programs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 17}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 188}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AFFORDABLE HOUSING SCREEN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Affordable Housing Screen is a digital interface used to determine loan limits and eligibility for affordable housing programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Affordable Housing Screen is a system interface used by lenders to verify income limits and other important details related to affordable housing financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;APPRAISAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Appraisal is an assessment conducted to determine the current market value of a property, which is crucial for mortgage lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"An Appraisal is an assessment of the value of a property, which is necessary for lenders to determine the amount of money they will provide for a loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal is a process where a property's value is assessed by a professional appraiser, often required for mortgage transactions to ensure loan amounts align with property value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal refers to the evaluation of a property's value, which must be dated within a certain period before closing, as per loan guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal is an event that assesses the value of a property to ensure the loan amount aligns with the property’s market value."&lt;SEP&gt;"An appraisal is an evaluation of a property's value that is required for Jumbo Desk Reviews, with specific conditions based on loan amounts and product requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal is an event in the mortgage process where the property's market value is evaluated to determine loan amounts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal is a professional assessment aimed at determining the value of a property, which is crucial in the mortgage lending process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Appraisal is an evaluation of the property's value conducted by a professional appraiser which is required for qualifying for a loan as per program requirements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b75506a7175a05b7c26944fe1aa93eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4b9e8302b8de2d8d692106e4e284ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-283d5323d92a66b703dacfb0b3c98a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6a7f245e88177bac6b85d5f808ebd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42979d97c1c73c1b28eac498c9aee682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-192e3f9f08a0121645e56ca36babd81b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0908ef3e42a9d0bcd40742960e19dbf2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 89}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 443}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME LIMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income Limit refers to the maximum income level a borrower can have to qualify for certain loan products, often based on AMI."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BORROWER NAME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Borrower Name is a term referencing the individual or entity obtaining the loan, signifying their involvement in the transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrower Name refers to the individual or entity applying for the loan, whose financial information must be verified through documentation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Borrower Name refers to the individuals who apply for a mortgage loan, as identified in the documentation and underwriting support information."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25a82bf13c8c6a8ef98d1a15a5361ea9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 22}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 222}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENOVATIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Renovations refer to improvements or upgrades made to a property, which are often relevant for determining financing limits under mortgage loan programs like HomeReady."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNDERWRITING SUPPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Underwriting Support includes assistance provided by Flagstar or other institutions for processing FHA loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Support is a service or team within a lending institution that assists in the processing and evaluation of mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Support operates to verify and document borrower information, ensuring compliance with mortgage lending standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Support refers to assistance and resources provided to ensure loans are processed and approved in accordance with regulations and guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Support refers to the assistance provided in evaluating and approving mortgage applications, as indicated by the contact email associated with Flagstar Bank."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Support is the department at Flagstar that assists with the correction of documentation discrepancies during the underwriting process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Support signifies assistance provided in the underwriting process, ensuring compliance with established guidelines and criteria."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fe4b9e8302b8de2d8d692106e4e284ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf2d9f6b5b471373ca78f75c11d02725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da6a7f245e88177bac6b85d5f808ebd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662a2c10d200da7291e0212d33749544</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 430}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PURCHASE MORTGAGE LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Purchase Mortgage Loans are loans used specifically to buy a home, which may be subject to educational requirements for borrowers in programs such as HomeReady."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RATE/TERM REFINANCE TRANSACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rate/Term Refinance Transactions are types of refinancing that involve adjusting the interest rate or term of an existing mortgage without cashing out equity."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 374}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINIMUM BORROWER CONTRIBUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minimum Borrower Contribution outlines the required funds that a borrower must contribute towards the transaction, as dictated by guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minimum Borrower Contribution refers to the least amount of funds a borrower must contribute from personal resources towards the purchase of a property to qualify for certain loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minimum Borrower Contribution refers to the predetermined amount that a borrower must contribute to a mortgage transaction, which involves various eligibility criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minimum Borrower Contribution refers to the required initial investment that a borrower must provide when securing a mortgage, often varying by loan product and property type."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minimum Borrower Contribution outlines the required initial investment a borrower must make to qualify for specific mortgage products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Minimum Borrower Contribution refers to the lowest amount of money the borrower is required to put down on a mortgage loan, as specified by lending guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfcbc01d9662fc8a4930eb1a9dd46384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-930f40233ddc622409d80debbd41e55f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3f42cc9266dff615db2fd5cb59e3109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 198}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 710}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME LIMITS DISPLAYED&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income Limits Displayed refer to the specific financial thresholds outlined in the application processes that define eligibility for loan products based on borrower income."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 202}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SCREENING PROCESS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Screening Process refers to the procedures used to evaluate a borrower's financial situation, including creditworthiness and income verification during loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 430}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FANNIE MAE WEBSITE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Fannie Mae Website is the online platform where borrowers and lenders can access information, tools, and resources related to mortgage financing and eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 373}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FEDERAL INFORMATION PROCESSING STANDARD (FIPS)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Federal Information Processing Standard (FIPS) is a standard for classifying geographic areas and is critical for assessing income limits in mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 85}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 429}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME VALIDATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income Validation Requirements refer to the specific documentation and evidence necessary to confirm income levels for mortgage applicants."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b8df18a65c5f6957ed36a347cf3c092</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 68}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 373}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CASH ON HAND&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cash on Hand refers to liquid funds that a borrower has available for down payment, closing costs, and prepaid expenses in a mortgage transaction, which must be verified for authenticity and sufficiency."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash on hand refers to liquid funds available to a borrower, typically used as part of the financial assessment when applying for a mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash on Hand refers to the amount of liquid funds available to a borrower, which is used to assess their eligibility for closing a loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd698c420bb978f364630c455d2abf4a</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 236}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PREVIOUS PAYMENT PRACTICES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Previous Payment Practices refer to the historical financial behavior of a borrower, especially regarding their use of cash and credit which can influence loan approval decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTERESTED PARTY CONTRIBUTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interested Party Contributions are funds provided by parties with vested interests in a real estate transaction, such as sellers or builders, designed to assist borrowers with closing costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interested Party Contributions are funds provided by related parties to help cover costs associated with closing a real estate transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interested Party Contributions encompass funds added by parties who have an interest in a real estate transaction, meant to cover specific costs in the loan process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 199}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 715}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BOARDER INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Boarder Income refers to rent income from individuals living with a borrower that may be included in qualifying income under certain conditions, as defined by Fannie Mae guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Boarder Income refers to rental income from individuals living with the borrower that can contribute to qualifying income under specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 266}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-BORROWER HOUSEHOLD INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-Borrower Household Income is income generated by individuals living with a borrower who is not part of the loan application but can have implications for financial assessments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 698}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SECONDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Seconds are a form of down payment assistance loans secured by the property, which may or may not be forgiven at the end of the loan term."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds are financing programs approved by HUD to assist low-income individuals in purchasing homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds are programs aimed at providing funds for eligible homebuyers, subsidizing subordinate financing for homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds are programs that provide second mortgage financing to low-to-moderate income families for purchasing homes, often as part of a larger effort to promote affordable housing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds refers to eligible subordinate financing programs from state, local, or municipal authorities, or nonprofit organizations to assist borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds are second mortgage products designed to assist low- and moderate-income borrowers in financing the purchase of homes, often with favorable terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds are subordinate financing options that may assist homebuyers in affording a down payment or purchase price, often linked to local housing programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds is a financing option that allows borrowers to obtain additional financing for homes with conditions on primary residence use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds is a type of second mortgage designed to assist borrowers with down payment needs, used in conjunction with first mortgage products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds are subsidized financing options provided by certain entities to assist borrowers with down payments or closing costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds refer to subsidized subordinate financing options that can be obtained from various entities to assist with mortgage costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds are financial assistance programs aimed at helping borrowers with second mortgage options for down payments or closing costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds represent funding programs from various entities that assist buyers by providing subordinate financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12641cd1a4c93cf93c1aa31082da47b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7de83587d951a7ec74fcb94d81a7df71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a675c08f3177636cb84734aead2aea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdba698a5ff7dd259797f2300b8f4759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 585}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 834}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ACCESSORY UNIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Accessory Unit is an additional living space in a property that can potentially generate rental income, playing a role in qualifying a borrower for a mortgage."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 266}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL ESTATE TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">("EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Real Estate Transaction encompasses the process of transferring property ownership, involving various parties including buyers, sellers, and lenders, with specific considerations for financing and costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate Transaction encompasses the process of buying, selling, or transferring ownership of property, involving various parties and legal considerations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate Transaction refers to the process of buying or selling property, which involves various financial arrangements including down payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate Transaction refers to the process of buying, selling, or transferring ownership of real estate assets."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Real Estate Transaction involves the sale or transfer of property ownership, including the potential financing mechanisms and negotiations involved."&lt;SEP&gt;"Real Estate Transaction is the process of buying, selling, or leasing property, which includes various legal and financial procedures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ca3069902295dcf5b2b505753d7623f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25dcfc163b5b00ffab734b755ea03592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 717}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ASSETS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Assets refer to any resources owned by a borrower that can serve as collateral or proof of financial stability when applying for a mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assets refer to resources owned by an individual or household, which can be used to secure loans or demonstrate financial stability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assets refer to financial resources and reserves that must be documented per industry guidelines to qualify for a mortgage or loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a675c08f3177636cb84734aead2aea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 30}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RISK/TERM REFINANCE TRANSACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Risk/Term Refinance Transactions involve refinancing existing loans where borrowers may seek to adjust the terms of their mortgage to reduce payments or access cash."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 189}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 681}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINIMUM CONTRIBUTION REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minimum Contribution Requirement is the least amount of money a borrower must contribute towards a real estate transaction, as mandated by lending institutions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 698}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RESERVES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reserves are the funds that borrowers must have available after closing costs to ensure they can handle future mortgage payments and expenses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserves refer to additional funds that a borrower must have available as a cushion for unexpected expenses after closing a mortgage transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserves refer to the amount of savings that a borrower must have on hand after closing, which can vary based on loan-to-value ratio requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserves refer to the savings or assets that a borrower must maintain to demonstrate their ability to cover mortgage payments beyond their regular income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserves refer to the additional funds required by lenders to ensure that borrowers can continue to make payments in case of unforeseen circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a403e885ce18327dd600e7521b66a2e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 63}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 354}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documentation involves filing and providing necessary evidence to support financial claims, such as proof of income or identity, during the mortgage application process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation refers to the collection of forms and records necessary to complete the application process for down payment assistance programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation refers to the required paperwork and legal documents necessary for processing mortgage applications and closing transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation refers to the necessary paperwork required for loan processing, determining loan eligibility and status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation is a critical industry process that involves gathering, validating, and utilizing necessary records and proofs for financial transactions, especially in lending and mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation refers to the necessary records and proofs that validate a borrower's financial information when applying for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation refers to various forms and evidence required to satisfy lending guidelines, including financial statements and appraisals."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72060811d2de811b03ec94848dcad94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d99ce4642f1e6e8c39678043a90b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3069902295dcf5b2b505753d7623f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150cc6b2e7ba7007f09ed79ae5042c88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 267}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT REPORT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A credit report is a detailed record of an individual's credit history used by lenders to assess creditworthiness and make lending decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Report is a detailed summary of an individual's credit history used by lenders to evaluate creditworthiness when applying for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Report is a record of an individual's credit history that lenders review to determine eligibility for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Report is a detailed account of a borrower's credit history, used by lenders to assess creditworthiness and loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Report is a document detailing an individual's credit history, which lenders use to evaluate creditworthiness when underwriting loans, including HELOCs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit reports are necessary documents in the process of evaluating borrowers for HELOC eligibility, vital for approval decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Report is a comprehensive record of an individual's credit history, used by lenders to determine loan eligibility and terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Credit Report is the financial document that contains information about a person's credit history, which is critical for lenders assessing loan eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5c2f4d692a0955d46073163734c23b26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd698c420bb978f364630c455d2abf4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df57131d49eba22a5ca15cafeb404cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aade21d11a3ffb0d61652426f005667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-930f40233ddc622409d80debbd41e55f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150cc6b2e7ba7007f09ed79ae5042c88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 30}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 245}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENTAL INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rental Income is income derived from renting property, and it is explicitly deemed ineligible for certain loan qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to funds earned by renting out a property or part of a property, which can be considered in mortgage qualification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to earnings generated from leasing out property, which can impact a borrower's mortgage eligibility under Freddie Mac guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to earnings derived from leasing property, which can be considered when qualifying for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rental Income refers to the earnings derived from renting out property, which can be considered in assessing a borrower's financial eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5c2f4d692a0955d46073163734c23b26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec9b17609d27a36004f6e85b0cb3ecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a403e885ce18327dd600e7521b66a2e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d2fd985d041d5eb6aeccbb1d21a81c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 189}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 681}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STANDARD GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Standard Guidelines are broadly accepted principles that govern the documentation and processes required for mortgage transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DRIVER'S LICENSE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Driver's License serves as a commonly accepted form of identification and address verification for individuals involved in rental agreements and mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BILL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Bill is a statement of charges from a service provider that can serve as proof of residency for mortgage-related documentation."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BANK STATEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Bank Statement is a financial document that summarizes a person's banking activity, used to support income verification in mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SECONDS PROGRAMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Community Seconds Programs are initiatives designed to provide additional financing options for low- to moderate-income homebuyers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds Programs are initiatives that provide second mortgages to assist low-to-moderate income families with home purchases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community Seconds Programs specifically refer to loan structures designed for providing down payment assistance secured by property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 152}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 615}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FINANCIAL INSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A financial institution is an entity that accepts deposits from the public and provides loans and credit, playing a crucial role in the mortgage process regarding funds for down payments and closing costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial Institution refers to a bank or lender that provides financial services including loans, mortgages, and deposits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial Institutions are entities, such as banks or credit unions, that provide financial services including mortgage lending and verifying borrower credentials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial Institution refers to banks or other entities that provide financial services, including lending and credit assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial Institution refers to banks, credit unions, and other organizations that provide financial services, including lending."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd698c420bb978f364630c455d2abf4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3069902295dcf5b2b505753d7623f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb4e4bbf1091286e7015a8784c37cbc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150cc6b2e7ba7007f09ed79ae5042c88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 33}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 259}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONTRIBUTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contributions refer to financial contributions that may be applied to reduce mortgage costs, such as interest rates and closing costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contributions refer to funds provided by parties involved in the real estate transaction to assist the borrower in covering costs."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 235}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Guidelines refer to a set of rules or instructions provided for the administration of down payment assistance programs and their requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guidelines refer to established procedures and rules that govern the mortgage lending process and help ensure compliance with regulatory standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guidelines refer to the set of rules and instructions established by organizations like Flagstar to govern the approval and execution of financial programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guidelines refer to the principles and rules established by lending institutions to process applications and assess eligibility for loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdba698a5ff7dd259797f2300b8f4759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 545}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTATION STANDARDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documentation Standards are specific requirements set forth by lenders that dictate the necessary paperwork and information needed to support a mortgage application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 189}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 681}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN PROCEEDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Proceeds are the funds that a borrower receives from a lender after approving a mortgage application."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Proceeds refer to the funds received from a loan, which must be properly allocated and documented in real estate transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Proceeds represent the funds obtained through a loan, which must be allocated properly according to the terms of the mortgage agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b42b071e6198f2a53344eeed3e0dca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c977b52194d7751d347d7a9c63060b4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 199}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 714}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 853}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;STATEMENT OF INTENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Statement of Intent is a written declaration by a non-borrower household occupant indicating their intention to reside with the borrower for a specified period."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RENTAL INCOME GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rental Income Guidelines refer to the specific criteria set by lending institutions outlining how rental income can be used in qualifying a borrower."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 266}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;QUALIFIED INCOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Qualified Income refers to the income verified by documentation that is acceptable for determining loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Qualified Income refers to the specific income sources that meet the requirements set by lenders for using in mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8ec9b17609d27a36004f6e85b0cb3ecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 698}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSACTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transaction refers to the process of conducting business or financial dealings between parties, commonly in real estate and lending contexts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transaction refers to the transfer of value between parties, crucial in loan processes, especially during refinancing or the purchase of property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b42b071e6198f2a53344eeed3e0dca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
