</node>
<node id="&quot;DOCUMENTATION REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Documentation Requirements are the necessary paperwork and information a Borrower must provide to facilitate the mortgage application process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements are the specific conditions that must be met regarding paperwork in the mortgage application process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation requirements are the set of necessary papers and forms that borrowers must provide to lenders to verify their identities and financial capabilities when applying for a mortgage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements refer to the various forms and proofs that borrowers must submit to validate their financial standing and transaction viability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation requirements refer to the required paperwork needed to complete FHA loan applications and ensure compliance with guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements are the specific papers and evidence needed to support a borrower's loan application, ensuring compliance with lending standards."&lt;SEP&gt;"Documentation Requirements entail the necessary papers and records that borrowers must provide to support their loan applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd698c420bb978f364630c455d2abf4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3069902295dcf5b2b505753d7623f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-803513d6e632c311aec48592cb79b4f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5c9771e9d7f170cab82a4f6e0fe9c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7240c801a08e04a5a9db69a7879361cf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 36}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 265}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 775}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MINIMUM AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Minimum Amount refers to the baseline figure that a borrower must contribute towards various costs or payments during the loan process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 192}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 698}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CREDIT USAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Credit Usage refers to how a borrower utilizes credit, which can affect their credit score and lending eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONG-TERM RESIDENCY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Long-Term Residency is a condition where an occupant has lived at an address for an extended period, providing stability and reliability to their income claims."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 19}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 189}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 681}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TRANSACTION COSTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Transaction Costs are all expenses involved in executing a real estate transaction beyond the property price, including fees for services and paperwork."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-db88d357021738de0f589ce49936e0e1</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 199}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 714}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 853}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TEXAS CONSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Texas Constitution is referenced in relation to refinance loan evaluations and legal requirements in Texas."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Texas Constitution outlines specific requirements for refinancing loans in Texas, particularly under Section 50(a)(6) relating to borrower protections and criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Texas Constitution outlines the legal framework governing properties and mortgages in Texas, specifically referenced in relation to home refinances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c977b52194d7751d347d7a9c63060b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 14}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 157}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEREST PARTY CONTRIBUTION LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest Party Contribution Limits refer to the set maximum percentages that can be contributed by interested parties towards closing costs, varying by the loan's combined loan-to-value (CLTV) ratio."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 201}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE INSURANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mortgage Insurance is a financial product required for certain loans, often tied to the loan-to-value ratio, protecting lenders against borrower default."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance refers to insurance that protects lenders against losses due to borrower default, which is often required for loans with a higher Loan-to-Value (LTV) ratio."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a policy that protects lenders against the risk of borrower default, typically required for loans with a high LTV ratio."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance refers to insurance that protects lenders against defaults on loans, which can impact escrow waivers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance provides financial protection for lenders, with specific guidelines for obtaining and maintaining coverage during construction loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is insurance that protects the lender in case a borrower defaults on their loan, often required for loans with a lower down payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage insurance is an insurance policy that protects lenders against borrower default on a mortgage loan, separate from title insurance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a type of insurance that protects lenders against default on mortgages, typically required for loans over 80% LTV."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a financial product that protects lenders against losses due to borrower default, often required for loans with lower down payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a type of insurance that protects lenders against losses from default on a mortgage loan, having specific guidelines in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a form of protection for lenders against losses due to mortgage default, often required for loans with lower down payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a financial product that protects lenders against borrower default, mentioned in relation to the Fannie Mae HomeReady guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a type of insurance intended to protect lenders from losses due to defaults on loans, relevant for borrowers under the HomeReady program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is insurance required for loans above a certain LTV ratio, protecting the lender from potential losses in case of default."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a policy that protects lenders against borrower default, required in certain mortgage conditions.'&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance refers to the premium payments made to insure lenders against default on FHA-insured mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is not required under the Advantage program, which can affect borrowing qualifications and costs for homeowners."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Insurance is a policy that protects lenders against loss if a borrower defaults on a loan, typically required for loans with low down payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2292650099ea1cdf5881f79ed28d3cfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72060811d2de811b03ec94848dcad94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593f9403b246f17722c284b9fc562c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3f42cc9266dff615db2fd5cb59e3109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9351b24bca225d97ff2d45b46310a878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8760dceb193fd7c5f24d24209ee5e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a577e8766cf4f0e1ae599795cd9c6fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0908ef3e42a9d0bcd40742960e19dbf2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 139}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 577}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIMARY RESIDENCES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Primary Residences are homes that are occupied by the borrower as their main dwelling, serving as the basis for various lending guidelines and requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residences are properties that serve as the main home for a residential borrower, with specific lending parameters outlined for qualifying."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 717}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEW YORK PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"New York Properties are real estate in New York that may have specific underwriting guidelines as indicated in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"New York Properties are referenced within the guidelines but require adherence to specific underwriting criteria as outlined in the Conventional Underwriting Guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"New York Properties refer to real estate located in New York that is subject to specific lending guidelines for mortgage eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 11}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 140}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 579}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBORDINATE FINANCING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Subordinate Financing indicates additional loans that can be obtained in conjunction with the principal loan, specified in the context of the mortgage products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing involves secondary loans taken out against a property in addition to the primary mortgage, often to cover down payment or closing costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to additional financing options that may be used alongside the primary loan, affecting property types and loan limits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to additional loans that are secured against the same property but after the primary mortgage, typically used to help with the down payment or covering closing costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to secondary loans taken out against a property that already has a primary mortgage, which may not be allowed in certain cases."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to secondary loans taken out against a property that rank below the primary loan, influencing loan amount eligibility and approval processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate financing refers to financing that is secondary to primary loans and is mentioned as not allowed in specific lending guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to secondary loans taken against property, which can impact the title insurance coverage based on priority."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to any secondary loans taken out in addition to a primary mortgage, which impacts the repayment structure of the loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to secondary loans taken out against a property, which are subordinate in priority to the primary mortgage loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to financing obtained that is secondary to the primary mortgage, with specific eligibility references."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing involves additional loans that are secured against a property after the primary loan, often allowing for greater overall borrowing capacity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to an additional loan taken out against a property that is secondary to the primary mortgage, affecting the lending structure and risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to loans taken out after a primary loan secured against the same property, often utilized to facilitate additional borrowing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing is a financial structure where secondary loans are provided to assist in purchasing properties without exceeding limits set by primary lenders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to any additional loans secured by a property that are subordinate to the primary mortgage, impacting the Combined Loan-to-Value (CLTV) ratio."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subordinate Financing refers to secondary loans that are secured by a property, requiring specific criteria to be eligible, especially in relation to borrower's primary financing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b42b071e6198f2a53344eeed3e0dca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c977b52194d7751d347d7a9c63060b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc754fc30ff722a8fee09393323a03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8760dceb193fd7c5f24d24209ee5e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-060d3305d5697520404f94c4fcd2cb85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e572c9b9bd53e500c5e02283f3230e6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdba698a5ff7dd259797f2300b8f4759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 12}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 144}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 585}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 833}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BUILDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Builder is a person or company responsible for constructing properties, whose contributions may also be part of financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Builder refers to the entity involved in the construction process, which may play a role in financing and real estate transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Builders are contractors or construction professionals engaged in projects funded through Flagstar's construction loans, collaborating with borrowers and lenders."&lt;SEP&gt;"Builder refers to the entity or individual responsible for constructing properties, often requiring specific qualifications and oversight in loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Builder is a party involved in the real estate transaction, collaborating with sellers and buyers, who may also contribute to interested party contributions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-71f642eb6cc44e3fc724fd1b5beeccd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aade21d11a3ffb0d61652426f005667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25dcfc163b5b00ffab734b755ea03592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 20}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 200}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 716}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REAL ESTATE BROKER/AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Real Estate Broker/Agent refers to professionals who assist in buying, selling, or renting properties, often involved in facilitating transactions and guiding clients."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9</data>
