<node id="&quot;SPECIAL FEATURE CODES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Special Feature Codes are identifiers required for loan programs, ensuring specific features or characteristics are documented within loan files."&lt;SEP&gt;"Special Feature Codes are identifiers that must be included in loan documentation to indicate specific features or statuses of the loan product."&lt;SEP&gt;"Special Feature Codes are identifiers that categorically represent certain borrower characteristics related to mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Special Feature Codes are required codes attached to loan files to indicate the specific loan program features that need to be considered by underwriters."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0908ef3e42a9d0bcd40742960e19dbf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 118}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 527}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CLTV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) considers multiple mortgages secured against a property and affects a borrower's eligibility for financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV stands for Combined Loan-To-Value ratio, which is a calculation that assesses the ratio of all loans secured by a property to the property's appraised value."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV stands for Combined Loan-To-Value ratio, which is a financial term used to express the ratio of all loans secured by a property to its appraised value."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV stands for Combined Loan-To-Value ratio, which takes into account the total amount of loans secured against a property in relation to its value."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV, or Combined Loan-To-Value ratio, refers to the total amount of all loans secured by a property divided by the appraised value, impacting financing limits."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV, or Combined Loan to Value ratio, is a metric used to assess the risk of lending in relation to the value of the property and is critical in mortgage processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV, or Combined Loan-to-Value ratio, is a calculation of the total amount of loans secured by a property compared to its appraised value."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV, or Combined Loan-to-Value ratio, takes into account all loans secured by the property to calculate the overall risk of lending."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e01afc290e08ec0f3a536bcbc8c10f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25dcfc163b5b00ffab734b755ea03592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc754fc30ff722a8fee09393323a03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad5bfdaee64eed200866a097fc789e6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
