<node id="&quot;PREPAYMENT PENALTY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Prepayment Penalty is a fee charged to a borrower for paying off a loan before the agreed-upon time, typically included in mortgage agreements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prepayment Penalty is a fee that may be charged to a borrower who pays off a loan early, compensating the lender for lost interest."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prepayment Penalty is a financial term indicating that there is no penalty for early repayment of certain loans offered by Flagstar Bank."&lt;SEP&gt;"PREPAYMENT PENALTY refers to the conditions concerning charges that may apply if a borrower pays off a loan early."&lt;SEP&gt;"Prepayment Penalty is a fee that lenders may charge borrowers for paying off their loan early, which is not allowed in the Advantage program."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a72060811d2de811b03ec94848dcad94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593f9403b246f17722c284b9fc562c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45f29d1e5fffab173b878a2ce71c0888</data>
