<node id="&quot;SUPER CONFORMING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"SUPER CONFORMING refers to a category of loans that exceed the conforming limit but still qualify under certain guidelines for the Home Possible program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Super Conforming is a loan product that falls within a specific range above standard conforming loans but below the limits of Jumbo loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Super Conforming is a specific category of mortgage loan designed for higher-cost areas, allowing for higher loan limits than conventional loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Super Conforming refers to a category of mortgage products offered by Freddie Mac that allows higher loan limits compared to traditional conforming loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Super Conforming loans are designed for properties in high-cost areas, providing higher loan limits than conventional conforming loans under the Home Possible program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Super Conforming refers to a type of mortgage that exceeds the conforming loan limits but adheres to certain government guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f626d237ebaf21492fcd8cbd9a81536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304d9428ac3f0546fe2c83618fb493e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a582fe17fe66be19c89056580dbaccc</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 4}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 74}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FHA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"FHA refers to the Federal Housing Administration, and sellers may require separate approval from Flagstar to participate in FHA-related mortgage programs."&lt;SEP&gt;FHA, also known as the Federal Housing Administration, is a United States government agency responsible for providing mortgage insurance on loans made by approved lenders. This agency plays a crucial role in the housing and mortgage markets by facilitating home financing, particularly for borrowers with low to moderate incomes. FHA loans are government-backed mortgages designed for low-to-moderate-income borrowers, offering lower minimum down payments and eligibility for programs like the Extended Lock with Float-Down. The main goal of FHA is to improve housing standards, conditions, and to provide an adequate home financing system. FHA-approved lenders can offer both fixed- and adjustable-rate mortgages to borrowers, ultimately enabling more affordable housing options across the U.S.&lt;SEP&gt;"FHA refers to the Federal Housing Administration, which insures loans, allowing lenders to offer lower down payments and interest rates, thereby assisting home buyers."&lt;SEP&gt;"FHA refers to the Federal Housing Administration, which insures loans, allowing lenders to offer lower down payments and interest rates."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4b9e8302b8de2d8d692106e4e284ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30274d85a38f031223e249148db13d86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f626d237ebaf21492fcd8cbd9a81536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4bffe67af21dcc27a55a8935b91a11c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717a880d45de770514dc0429a3dc79f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f5bfa76be42aa009ba16638227f047&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f214a47f3746b540cbee12f81aa5bc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8760dceb193fd7c5f24d24209ee5e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82a675c08f3177636cb84734aead2aea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdba698a5ff7dd259797f2300b8f4759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 107}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 475}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 820}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;VA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) offers various loan programs and benefits to eligible veterans, helping them secure financing for homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"VA loans are guaranteed by the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs, designed to benefit military veterans with favorable loan terms and are included in the Extended Lock with Float-Down programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"VA refers to the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs, which provides various financial and other benefits to eligible military veterans and their families, including loan guarantees."&lt;SEP&gt;"VA refers to the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs, and sellers may require separate approval to provide VA loans through Flagstar."&lt;SEP&gt;"VA refers to the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs, which offers loans and benefits to veterans and active-duty service members."&lt;SEP&gt;"VA refers to the United States Department of Veterans Affairs, which provides loan benefits to veterans and active military, pertinent to the eligibility focus of the document."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b75506a7175a05b7c26944fe1aa93eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4b9e8302b8de2d8d692106e4e284ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f626d237ebaf21492fcd8cbd9a81536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717a880d45de770514dc0429a3dc79f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f214a47f3746b540cbee12f81aa5bc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdba698a5ff7dd259797f2300b8f4759</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 81}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 409}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 806}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;USDA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The USDA is the United States Department of Agriculture, a government agency that provides various loan programs aimed at improving housing options in rural areas, promoting homeownership, and supporting community development."&lt;SEP&gt;"USDA loans are government-backed loans for rural development, aimed at promoting homeownership in less densely populated areas, and eligible for the Extended Lock with Float-Down."&lt;SEP&gt;"USDA refers to a government-backed mortgage program for rural development included in the pricing information."&lt;SEP&gt;"USDA refers to the United States Department of Agriculture, which provides various services and assistance programs for rural housing, also involved in mortgage loans across rural areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"USDA refers to the United States Department of Agriculture, which provides various services and assistance programs for rural housing."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f626d237ebaf21492fcd8cbd9a81536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4bffe67af21dcc27a55a8935b91a11c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13f5bfa76be42aa009ba16638227f047</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 22}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 221}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 764}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADVANTAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Advantage appears to be an organization related to lending or mortgage guidelines, which outlines various financial and credit protocols."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage is a financial entity that provides mortgage and refinancing options for primary residences, second homes, and investments, focusing on various loan types and criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage is a financial product offering various loan options including fixed and adjustable-rate mortgages, aimed at expanded eligibility for home buyers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage is an organization or program that provides specific guidelines for student loan payments and borrower qualifications, facilitating the process for individuals seeking financial assistance in education."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage is described in the context as an organization or program that outlines specific guidelines for student loan payments and borrower qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage refers to a financial organization that provides mortgage and credit product guidelines, focusing on credit requirements and borrower eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage refers to a specific type of loan product that is listed as ineligible for the float-down renegotiation policy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage refers to a type of loan product that is ineligible for the Extended Lock with Float-Down program, indicating certain restrictions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5c2f4d692a0955d46073163734c23b26&lt;SEP&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f626d237ebaf21492fcd8cbd9a81536&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150cc6b2e7ba7007f09ed79ae5042c88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af318020d8f16430d1a60515a789d41d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7240c801a08e04a5a9db69a7879361cf</data>
