  <data key="d1">"Maximum CLTV refers to the cap on the combined loan-to-value ratio for a borrower, ensuring that the total loan amount does not exceed a specified percentage of the property's value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum CLTV, or combined loan-to-value ratio, outlines the total ratio of loans secured by the property relative to its value, factoring into loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"The maximum CLTV is specified along with the maximum HCLTV, both determining financing limits for eligible borrowers."</data>
