  <data key="d1">"Desktop Underwriter (DU) determines qualifying ratios as part of the assessment process for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Qualifying Ratios are financial ratios used by lenders to determine a borrower's ability to repay a loan, which includes debt-to-income ratios."&lt;SEP&gt;"Qualifying Ratios are metrics used to evaluate a borrower's ability to repay a mortgage, often calculated based on debt-to-income ratios."&lt;SEP&gt;"Qualifying Ratios are financial formulas used by lenders to determine a borrower's ability to repay their mortgage based on debt-to-income ratios."&lt;SEP&gt;"Qualifying Ratios are financial measures used to assess a borrower's eligibility for an FHA loan based on income and debt levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Qualifying Ratios are financial benchmarks used to evaluate a borrower's ability to repay a loan based on their income and expenses."</data>
