<node id="&quot;ADVANTAGE BANK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Advantage Bank is a financial institution providing guidelines and requirements for eligible borrowers and property types in mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage Bank is a financial institution that offers a variety of loan products, primarily focused on mortgage lending and providing financial services to individuals and businesses in need of financing for real estate transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage Bank is a financial institution that offers various types of loans, including fixed rate and adjustable rate loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage Bank is a financial institution that provides various loan products and refinances options for primary and secondary residences, with specific terms regarding loan-to-value ratios and credit scores."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage Bank is characterized as a lending institution that offers a variety of mortgage financing options, including cash-out refinances and purchase loans with specific criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage Bank is mentioned as a financial institution involved in the processing of closing documents and specific loan guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Advantage Bank is mentioned in the context of providing product guidelines and transaction types for loans and refinancing."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c977b52194d7751d347d7a9c63060b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0bf252dda6ffda0104c759447cefbb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-076af9e929f806725a98e51a239feee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c57c1331aa9873de4467468c1b07505</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 345}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PRIMARY RESIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Primary Residence describes the main dwelling of a borrower, differentiating loan terms based on whether the property is a primary living space."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residence is defined as the main home where the borrower lives, significant in determining mortgage eligibility and requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residence is the main dwelling where a borrower lives, significantly impacting their eligibility for certain financing options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residence is the main home where a borrower lives, usually featuring distinctive mortgage conditions and benefits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Primary Residence refers to a type of mortgage product that offers purchase and refinance options based on various criteria such as loan amount and credit score."&lt;SEP&gt;PRIMARY RESIDENCE is the main dwelling where a borrower resides, qualifying for specific loan benefits and influencing the terms and conditions of mortgage loans. It is the key consideration in mortgage applications and requirements, denoting the main home where the borrower lives, and has implications for various types of loan transactions. This classification is relevant in the context of property loans, refinancing options, and eligibility for different financing conditions. Additionally, PRIMARY RESIDENCE plays a significant role in determining mortgage eligibility for various programs such as Home Possible, Home Equity Line of Credit, and HomeReady loans. Ultimately, it is required for specific loan types under FHA guidelines and is essential for eligibility in refinancing.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-930f40233ddc622409d80debbd41e55f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6de80860713bbcd40afb3b3b69d1945f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8760dceb193fd7c5f24d24209ee5e31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b06bf2c39f8da79b3399842638c80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150cc6b2e7ba7007f09ed79ae5042c88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b75506a7175a05b7c26944fe1aa93eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f18d8da3052c73dc1f9fa6e9aef1a14e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f28aa24c80be0008755d728b5169b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0459e9b5b3885ad40728e4e0af01123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a582fe17fe66be19c89056580dbaccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c977b52194d7751d347d7a9c63060b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3069902295dcf5b2b505753d7623f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a403e885ce18327dd600e7521b66a2e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc754fc30ff722a8fee09393323a03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c57c1331aa9873de4467468c1b07505</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 62}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 345}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SECOND HOME&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Second Home is a type of residential property that is purchased primarily as an additional option for living arrangements, often applied for leisure use."&lt;SEP&gt;"A Second Home refers to a property owned in addition to a primary residence, often used for vacation or temporary stays."&lt;SEP&gt;"SECOND HOME is a term used for properties that serve as a secondary residence, which are also eligible for various refinancing options with specific lending criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"SECOND HOME refers to financing related to properties that are not primary residences, with specific loan-to-value ratios and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to a property that is not the primary residence but is owned by the borrower for personal use or vacation purposes, subject to different lending criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to an additional residence typically used for vacation or leisure, impacting loan terms and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"SECOND HOME refers to a residential property that is not the primary residence of the owner, typically used for vacation or rental purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"SECOND HOME refers to a property that is used occasionally and is not the primary residence, often relevant in mortgage applications for vacation homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to a property that a buyer acquires in addition to their primary residence for occasional use or investment."&lt;SEP&gt;"SECOND HOME denotes an additional property type outlined in the document for which similar mortgage products are available, different from the primary residence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home is a type of property classified for financing, indicating a separate residence from the primary one."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to properties designated for part-time or vacation use, distinct from primary residences and with specific mortgage guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home indicates a classification for properties that are not the primary residence but are used for personal enjoyment or vacation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home is a type of property that serves as a secondary dwelling for the owner, generally different from their primary place of residence."&lt;SEP&gt;"SECOND HOME refers to additional residences that may also be eligible for the Home Equity Line of Credit under specific terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to a mortgage product designed for individuals purchasing a secondary residence, with distinct refinancing options and loan criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to a supplementary property that borrowers occupy for leisure or vacation purposes, subject to specific loan guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home indicates a residence that is not the primary home, which can have different lending criteria compared to primary properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Second Home refers to properties that are not the primary residence, which may have different lending requirements as each loan program specifies."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b75506a7175a05b7c26944fe1aa93eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bc9ce80658e51e7fed2cac493270e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304d9428ac3f0546fe2c83618fb493e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad5bfdaee64eed200866a097fc789e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25dcfc163b5b00ffab734b755ea03592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f28aa24c80be0008755d728b5169b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42979d97c1c73c1b28eac498c9aee682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c57c1331aa9873de4467468c1b07505</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 316}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PURCHASE AND RATE/TERM REFINANCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Purchase and Rate/Term Refinance is an event referring to the processes through which borrowers can obtain financing options for buying homes or restructuring existing loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Purchase and Rate/Term Refinance refers to actions involving buying a property and refinancing existing loans, covered under mortgage product conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 56}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 316}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CONDO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A condo refers to a type of housing unit within a building or complex, mentioned as a property type eligible for financing under the HomeReady program."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo is a term for a condominium, a building or complex with individually owned units, often featuring shared communal areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo is a type of property classification listed in the mortgage guidelines, specifically referring to a condominium, which is a part of an apartment complex that is owned individually."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo is a type of residential property where individuals own a unit within a multi-unit complex while sharing common areas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo refers to a type of residential property ownership that is included in mortgage lending options, typically involving certain regulations and limits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo refers to a type of residential property that is individually owned but shares common areas with other units, impacting the terms and conditions of mortgage financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo refers to a condominium, a type of residential property that is individually owned but shares common areas with other units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo refers to a type of property specified for mortgage eligibility in the document, indicating condominiums as viable residential options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo refers to a condominium, a privately owned unit within a larger building or complex, which often shares common areas with other units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo refers to a condominium, which is a type of real estate property often included in mortgage insurance offerings, allowing individual ownership of units within a larger complex."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo refers to a type of property ownership in which individuals own individual units within a larger building or complex, often associated with shared amenities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo refers to a condominium, a type of residential property where individuals own individual units within a larger building or complex."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo is a type of residential property ownership involving individual ownership of units within a larger complex, with specific mortgage criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Condo is short for condominium, a type of housing where residents own individual units but share common areas."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304d9428ac3f0546fe2c83618fb493e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6de80860713bbcd40afb3b3b69d1945f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc754fc30ff722a8fee09393323a03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 326}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;CO-OP&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Co-op indicates cooperative housing as a property type listed in the mortgage products, where ownership is typically shared among residents."&lt;SEP&gt;"Co-op refers to a cooperative housing arrangement where residents own shares in a corporation that owns the property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Co-op stands for cooperative housing, which is another category of property applicable to leasing arrangements, included in various financing guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Co-op, or cooperative housing, refers to a housing arrangement where residents own shares of a corporation that owns the building, influencing the financing terms for potential buyers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Co-op refers to a type of housing cooperative that requires specific appraisal considerations and services for valuation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Co-op refers to cooperative housing arrangements assessed within the appraisal framework, with a fee of $75.00."&lt;SEP&gt;"Co-op stands for cooperative housing, where residents own shares in a corporation that owns the property, rather than owning their individual units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Co-op refers to a cooperative housing arrangement where residents own shares in a corporation that owns the building, affecting mortgage options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Co-op refers to cooperative housing arrangements where residents own shares in a corporation that owns the property and are allowed to occupy specific units."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37ad59fd9fe05a2fd14af3e367ff950d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f463e80705c368f56db31d1f00a4efe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 326}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Amount refers to the total monetary sum that a borrower receives from Flagstar for loans, upon which various fees are based."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Amount refers to the total value of money borrowed in a loan, a crucial factor in the comparison between loan programs described."&lt;SEP&gt;The "Loan Amount" refers to the total sum of money that can be borrowed by individuals from a lender to finance the purchase or construction of a property. This amount is subject to specific guidelines, calculations, and eligibility requirements, which vary based on property types and credit scores. It is a crucial term in mortgage scenarios, encompassing various tiers and conditions. The loan amount must be repaid over time, typically with interest, and is essential for processing, approvals, and determining insurance coverage. Additionally, in some cases, the loan amount borrowed from Flagstar is subject to EPD penalties if payments are delinquent. Ultimately, the loan amount is a financial term that influences eligibility and terms for mortgages, being the maximum amount that can be borrowed under specified conditions.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b722d926669aa7676c36ecbb75a4a233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9351b24bca225d97ff2d45b46310a878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662a2c10d200da7291e0212d33749544&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ae0a9048bf3b0256e59664fde5a07a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aade21d11a3ffb0d61652426f005667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1418f5447a956615e29938e7c6f0f71a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b75506a7175a05b7c26944fe1aa93eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0a48a482a40438f89f44e8758608310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77f9a0c774af974e032ea5bf1841d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c6c6dd97681ba9caa6c83d8ddf9ec59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3069902295dcf5b2b505753d7623f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25dcfc163b5b00ffab734b755ea03592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ae2131097a3957a665d280c4ed013cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f639d102461efe890e188cbc182dba52</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 59}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 333}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PROPERTY TYPE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Type categorizes the different types of properties eligible for construction loans, including single-unit, modular, and condominiums."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type distinguishes between various forms of real estate such as single-family homes, condos, and multi-unit buildings, affecting loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type refers to the classification of real estate involved in mortgage transactions, impacting financing conditions and requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type refers to the classification of the type of real estate property involved in a loan transaction, such as single-family homes, condos, or co-ops."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type refers to the classification of real estate properties for mortgage eligibility and includes various categories such as 1-Unit, 2-Unit, and investment properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type indicates the classification of the property (e.g., single-family home, condo), needed for loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type refers to the classification of real estate properties based on their characteristics, such as single-unit or multi-unit, relevant for financing eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type refers to the classification of the property involved in a loan, such as residential or commercial."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property type refers to the classification of real estate being financed, such as single-family homes, condominiums, or multi-unit properties, which impacts financing options and requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type is a classification criterion in mortgage lending that defines the kind of residential properties eligible for various loan products outlined in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type indicates the classification of the property being financed, which can affect loan terms and conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type is a classification referring to various categories of real estate, important in mortgage eligibility and terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Type relates to the classification of real estate used to determine eligibility and loan options in mortgage applications, including categories like residential, commercial, and mixed-use."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fd698c420bb978f364630c455d2abf4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b722d926669aa7676c36ecbb75a4a233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c6c6dd97681ba9caa6c83d8ddf9ec59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-060d3305d5697520404f94c4fcd2cb85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b36f295c3826a6aa7ec78dac1c05c756</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 58}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 326}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAXIMUM LOAN AMOUNT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maximum Loan Amount denotes the upper limit for various mortgage types, such as the $548,250 ceiling for Conventional Loan Programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum Loan Amount indicates the greatest amount of financing that can be approved for different types of loans based on property type and borrower qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum Loan Amount refers to the highest sum of money that can be borrowed under different loan types within the VA mortgage offerings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum Loan Amount refers to the upper limit set for borrowing against properties under specified lending programs, which varies by property type and location."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum Loan Amount refers to the upper limit of the loan that FHA may insure based on property type, income, and other factors."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1b06bf2c39f8da79b3399842638c80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb07e682734c9565708be6820699bc17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 107}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 476}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 825}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MAXIMUM LTV FOR PRIMARY RESIDENCE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maximum LTV for Primary Residence defines the highest allowable loan-to-value ratio for financing the primary home, which varies by property type."</data>
