</node>
<node id="&quot;ALTERNATIVE INCOME DOCUMENTATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Alternative Income Documentation refers to non-traditional methods of proving income for borrowers who may not have standard pay stubs or W-2s."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FIRST MORTGAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"First Mortgage is a primary loan taken to purchase real estate, against which other financial products, like HELOCs, are assessed."&lt;SEP&gt;"First Mortgage is the primary loan taken out to purchase a property, which may have specific guidelines impacting the approval of concurrent HELOCs."&lt;SEP&gt;"First Mortgage refers to the primary loan taken against a property, which has priority over any other liens or loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"First Mortgage refers to the primary loan taken against a property, which has priority over any secondary loans in the event of foreclosure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The First Mortgage refers to the primary loan secured by a property, often influencing the appraisal required for additional financing like a HELOC."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a8254e91bb361353c2efd5fd41f17e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd1c976503db6a0b9762d63aba656cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df57131d49eba22a5ca15cafeb404cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7de83587d951a7ec74fcb94d81a7df71</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 128}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 546}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;OWNERSHIP REQUIREMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Ownership Requirement refers to the stipulation for a borrower to have owned a property for a specified duration under mortgage guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;COMPLIANCE PROCEDURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Compliance Procedures are the regulations and practices that lenders must follow to ensure their loans adhere to legal standards and requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Compliance Procedures refers to protocols described in the document to ensure adherence to regulations surrounding escrow waivers."</data>
