</node>
<node id="&quot;SOFR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"SOFR or Secured Overnight Financing Rate is a benchmark interest rate used in the financial industry, particularly for determining rates on certain loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOFR, or Secured Overnight Financing Rate, is a benchmark interest rate used in financial markets, particularly for adjustable-rate mortgages."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOFR, or Secured Overnight Financing Rate, is a benchmark interest rate for dollar-denominated derivatives and loans, used as a standard for financial contracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOFR, or Secured Overnight Financing Rate, is a benchmark interest rate used in lending products such as those offered under the Home Possible program."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOFR, or Secured Overnight Financing Rate, is an interest rate benchmark used in adjustable-rate mortgages, reflecting secured overnight borrowing costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOFR, or Secured Overnight Financing Rate, is a benchmark interest rate used for financial products and serves as a reference for various financial transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOFR, or Secured Overnight Financing Rate, is a benchmark interest rate referenced in adjustable-rate loans, indicating expectations of market rates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a72060811d2de811b03ec94848dcad94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-357b3035e037e02a3c6636835c516347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f8738c76594c2ed9866d0e86818ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11f5ef3fffef89b593ca081411d1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2378deca7fb18f0144fa8707001424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6d8750d3b8676bc5099fb262793a7ff</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 105}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INDUSTRY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loans refer to borrowed money that is expected to be paid back with interest, often used to purchase property or fund real estate transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loans refer to the financial agreements provided by lenders to borrowers, which can be utilized for various purposes, including purchasing homes or paying off debts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loans refer to the financial products provided to borrowers, specifically related to mortgages for veterans in this context."&lt;SEP&gt;"The loans discussed are eligible for a float-down renegotiation policy and include conditions such as Approved with Conditions or Final Approval status to qualify."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af318020d8f16430d1a60515a789d41d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717a880d45de770514dc0429a3dc79f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01039c48e44ce5e4ea96c87117f23d78</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 63}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 350}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INTEREST ONLY LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest Only Loans allow borrowers to pay only the interest on the loan for a specified time, often leading to lower initial payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Only Loans are a type of mortgage where the borrower pays only the interest for a specific period, resulting in lower initial payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Only Loans are financial products that allow borrowers to pay only the interest on the loan for a specified period, which often leads to lower initial payments but higher long-term costs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Only Loans are financial products where borrowers pay only the interest for a certain period, making them potentially attractive for those looking to minimize initial payments."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f28aa24c80be0008755d728b5169b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d8141599e488921f66fe766d03ed3bf</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 63}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 351}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ELIGIBILITY GRIDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Eligibility Grids are charts or tables that establish criteria to determine the eligibility of loans based on factors like property type and credit score."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Grids are criteria charts used to assess the qualification of borrowers based on their financial profiles and other specific metrics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eligibility Grids are frameworks used to assess the qualifications of applicants for various loan products."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcbf025ce89296c2fe585617d648039b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 127}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 540}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;U.S. CITIZENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"U.S. Citizens are individuals eligible for certain borrowing guidelines as per Advantage Bank’s requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"U.S. Citizens are individuals who have legal citizenship in the United States and are eligible for certain financial products and loans as outlined in the guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"U.S. citizens are eligible borrowers for HELOCs, indicating their involvement in financial transactions involving home equity."&lt;SEP&gt;"U.S. citizens are identified as a category of eligible borrowers for the Home Equity Line of Credit."&lt;SEP&gt;"U.S. citizens are individuals eligible for financial transactions, often including home equity lines of credit (HELOCs), and play a significant role in the lending context."&lt;SEP&gt;"U.S. citizens are eligible borrowers for the FHA $100 HUD Repo program, allowing them to access low down payment loans for home purchases."&lt;SEP&gt;"U.S. Citizens are individuals recognized as legal members of the United States, eligible for various benefits including those related to mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"U.S. Citizens are individuals recognized as legal members of the United States, who have various rights and responsibilities, including those related to mortgage applications."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0bf252dda6ffda0104c759447cefbb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f28aa24c80be0008755d728b5169b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d10b59eabaab0b4bdac98f88233ce6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 127}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 540}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PERMANENT RESIDENT ALIENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Permanent Resident Aliens are non-citizens who are eligible for borrowing according to Advantage Bank's guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent Resident Aliens are non-citizens who have been granted the right to live and work permanently in the United States, qualifying for specific financial products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent resident aliens are eligible borrowers for HELOCs, showing their status in financial transactions relating to home equity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent resident aliens are identified as a category of eligible borrowers for the Home Equity Line of Credit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent resident aliens are also eligible borrowers for the FHA $100 HUD Repo program, enabling them to qualify for financing to buy homes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent resident aliens are eligible borrowers for FHA loans, listed among potential qualifying borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Permanent Resident Aliens are non-citizens who have been granted the right to reside permanently in the U.S., qualified to apply for home loans under specific guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0bf252dda6ffda0104c759447cefbb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f28aa24c80be0008755d728b5169b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d10b59eabaab0b4bdac98f88233ce6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 127}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 540}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NON-PERMANENT RESIDENT ALIENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Non-permanent Resident Aliens are individuals residing in the United States without permanent status, with specific eligibility for financial products as described in the guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-permanent Resident Aliens are temporary residents who must meet additional criteria for eligibility as borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-permanent resident aliens are identified as a category of eligible borrowers for the Home Equity Line of Credit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-permanent resident aliens qualify as eligible borrowers for HELOCs, indicating their participation in home financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-permanent resident aliens may qualify for the FHA $100 HUD Repo program depending on specific HUD guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-permanent resident aliens may qualify for FHA loans based on specific underwriting criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Non-permanent Resident Aliens are individuals who reside in the U.S. temporarily and possess specific qualifications for mortgage eligibility."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0bf252dda6ffda0104c759447cefbb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b0056b117b540a72b17dd275d006f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f28aa24c80be0008755d728b5169b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d10b59eabaab0b4bdac98f88233ce6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 127}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 544}]</data>
</node>
