<node id="&quot;PITIA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"PITIA refers to principal, interest, taxes, insurance, and association dues that borrowers must verify for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"PITIA stands for Principal, Interest, Taxes, Insurance, and Association dues, referring to the total monthly housing payment."&lt;SEP&gt;"PITIA stands for Principal, Interest, Taxes, Insurance, and Association dues, which are included in a borrower's housing payment and affect loan qualifications."&lt;SEP&gt;"PITIA stands for Principal, Interest, Taxes, Insurance, and Association Dues; it represents the total monthly housing expense used in loan assessments."&lt;SEP&gt;"PITIA stands for Principal, Interest, Taxes, Insurance, and Association Fees, outlining a borrower's monthly housing expenses considered in loan assessments."</data>
