</node>
<node id="&quot;MAXIMUM CASH OUT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Maximum Cash Out is the highest amount that a borrower can receive in cash from a loan, typically determined by the Loan-to-Value (LTV) ratio."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum Cash Out refers to the maximum amount a borrower can receive in cash back from a cash-out refinance, subject to specific loan criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maximum Cash Out specifies the upper limit on the amount of cash a borrower can receive through a cash-out refinance transaction."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42979d97c1c73c1b28eac498c9aee682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f</data>
