  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LTV (Loan-to-Value) Ratio is a financial calculation that measures the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, critical in determining lending risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Loan-to-Value (LTV) Ratio is a financial term that describes the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, typically used in mortgage underwriting."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-6f08c1849f1a1e52584c06fc2286667f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5</data>
