<node id="&quot;FORECLOSURE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Foreclosure is a legal process where a lender seeks to recover the balance of a loan from a borrower who has stopped making payments, often resulting in the sale of the property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Foreclosure refers to the legal process through which a lender takes possession of a property when the borrower fails to make payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Foreclosure is the legal process by which a lender takes possession of a property after the borrower defaults on a loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Foreclosure is a process where a lender takes possession of a property due to the owner's inability to make mortgage payments, categorized as a Housing Event."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8552c190e01cd6c887d540f68372a1a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30274d85a38f031223e249148db13d86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150cc6b2e7ba7007f09ed79ae5042c88</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 5}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 90}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 449}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;INCOME VERIFICATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Income Verification is the process described for confirming a borrower's income using various documents such as bank statements and W-2 forms for eligibility in mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income Verification is the process of confirming a borrower's income through documents like pay stubs, tax returns, or bank statements as part of the loan application process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income Verification is the process of confirming a borrower's income using various documents such as bank statements and W-2 forms for eligibility in mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Income Verification refers to the process through which lenders confirm a Borrower's income sources and amounts for mortgage qualification."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2315e50dabd40110b33a2bac5e271cc5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652c3091f21b7e8483d1309884976c82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5c9771e9d7f170cab82a4f6e0fe9c6</data>
