<node id="&quot;PROPERTY TYPES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Property Types are classifications of real estate that determine eligibility for mortgage loans under Advantage Bank’s guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Types encompass the various classifications of real estate, including single-family homes, multi-family homes, condominiums, and manufactured homes, each having distinct eligibility criteria for financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Types refer to the differing categories of real estate that can qualify for mortgage products, impacting eligibility and requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Types are classifications of real estate that determine eligibility for mortgage products, including one to four-unit properties and condominiums."&lt;SEP&gt;"Property Types categorize the different kinds of properties (e.g., single-family homes, condos, multi-family units) associated with loan products."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1b06bf2c39f8da79b3399842638c80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0bf252dda6ffda0104c759447cefbb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2378deca7fb18f0144fa8707001424</data>
