<node id="&quot;GIFT FUNDS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Gift Funds are a type of down payment assistance that consists of money given to the homebuyer without repayment obligations, typically sourced from family or non-profit organizations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift Funds are monetary contributions that can be used for down payments or closing costs under specific conditions, stipulating donor relationships and documentation requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift Funds are monetary gifts that may be used for down payments, subject to certain eligibility rules set by Advantage Bank."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gift Funds refer to monetary contributions from relatives that can be used for down payments or closing costs, with specific conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0bf252dda6ffda0104c759447cefbb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3069902295dcf5b2b505753d7623f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-437272f81cc4575a4fa57f55ce8d121c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-930f40233ddc622409d80debbd41e55f</data>
