<node id="&quot;DOWN PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Down Payment is the initial payment made by a borrower toward the purchase of a home, expressed as a percentage of the total sales price."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment is the initial payment made when purchasing a property, typically expressed as a percentage of the purchase price."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment refers to the initial upfront payment made by a homebuyer towards the purchase price of a property, often requiring assistance for funding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment is the initial upfront payment made by the borrower when purchasing a property, typically expressed as a percentage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Down Payment refers to the initial upfront payment made by the borrower when acquiring a property, crucial in the lending process."</data>
