<node id="&quot;DTI&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DTI (Debt-to-Income) measures an individual's monthly debt payments relative to their gross monthly income and is crucial in assessing loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"DTI, or Debt-To-Income ratio, is a key financial measurement discussed in the document, indicating the percentage of a borrower's income that goes towards servicing debt."&lt;SEP&gt;"DTI, or Debt-to-Income Ratio, is a financial metric used to determine a borrower's ability to manage monthly payments and is a factor in loan approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"DTI, or Debt-to-Income ratio, is a financial measure used by lenders to assess the borrower's ability to manage monthly payments and repay debts."&lt;SEP&gt;"DTI, or Debt-to-Income ratio, is a financial measure used to determine the percentage of a borrower's income that goes toward paying debts."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b75506a7175a05b7c26944fe1aa93eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c2f4d692a0955d46073163734c23b26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3f42cc9266dff615db2fd5cb59e3109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42979d97c1c73c1b28eac498c9aee682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c57c1331aa9873de4467468c1b07505</data>
