<node id="&quot;CLTV/HCLTV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) and HCLTV (Home Equity Combined Loan-to-Value) are financial ratios that represent the total amount of debt secured by a property divided by its appraised value."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV or Combined Loan-to-Value ratio is a financial metric that shows the ratio of all loans against a property compared to its appraised value."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV, or combined loan-to-value ratio, represents the total amount of loans secured by a property compared to its appraised value, important for mortgage approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV and HCLTV refer to Combined Loan-to-Value and Higher Combined Loan-to-Value ratios, determining the maximum allowable borrowing against property value in refinancing scenarios."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV/HCLTV refers to the loan-to-value ratios used in mortgage-related calculations, signifying the percentage of the total property value being financed."&lt;SEP&gt;"CLTV, or Combined Loan-to-Value, and HCLTV, or Home Equity Combined Loan-to-Value, are metrics used to evaluate loans, critical in assessing borrower eligibility for HomeReady products."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-92bc9ce80658e51e7fed2cac493270e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 57}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 323}]</data>
</node>
