<node id="&quot;UNDERWRITING ENGINE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Underwriting Engine is utilized in the process of evaluating and approving loan applications based on specified criteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Underwriting Engine refers to a digital system or software used to assess the risk of insuring a loan, evaluating the borrower's financial status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Engine is a technology used in evaluating the risk of insuring mortgages and determining eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Engine refers to automated systems that assess mortgage applications and provide output on loan eligibility and risk assessment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Engine is a term referring to the automated system used to assess the eligibility of mortgage applications for Home Possible loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Underwriting Engine used in the FHA lending process establishes guidelines and criteria for evaluating borrower applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Underwriting Engine refers to the software algorithms and processes used by lenders to assess the risk of lending to a borrower and to determine the approval of a loan."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5a582fe17fe66be19c89056580dbaccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e78a99763ca81ea2755a9310a0e6cc85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5d10b59eabaab0b4bdac98f88233ce6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fad5bfdaee64eed200866a097fc789e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55</data>
