</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN-TO-VALUE RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan-to-Value Ratio (LTV) is a financial metric that measures the ratio of a loan amount to the appraised value of an asset, often used in mortgage lending to determine risk and lending eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan-to-Value Ratio (LTV) is a financial term used by lenders to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan-to-Value Ratio (LTV) is a financial term used to determine risk, calculated by dividing the amount of the loan by the appraised value of the property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan-to-Value Ratio is a financial term comparing the amount of the mortgage loan to the appraised value of the property, used in lending decisions."</data>
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94010f4bdf2ece06575cf539272b8b45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3f42cc9266dff615db2fd5cb59e3109</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 7}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 96}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 454}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NUMBER OF FINANCED PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
