<node id="&quot;HELOC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HELOC (Home Equity Line of Credit) is a type of loan that uses the borrower's home as collateral, and specific title insurance requirements apply based on the loan amount."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC stands for Home Equity Line of Credit, a type of loan where the borrower can access funds based on the equity of their home."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC stands for Home Equity Line of Credit, which allows borrowers to access a revolving line of credit based on the equity in their home."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC, or Home Equity Line of Credit, is a financial product allowing homeowners to borrow against their equity, providing access to funds via a checkbook after closing."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC, or Home Equity Line of Credit, is a financial product that allows borrowers to access funds as needed, with specific guidelines and regulations surrounding its use."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC refers to a Home Equity Line of Credit, which has specific fees and policies regarding early payoff and the status of the line of credit."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC stands for Home Equity Line of Credit, allowing homeowners to borrow against their home equity for various financial needs, subject to specific conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"HELOC, or Home Equity Line of Credit, is a type of loan that allows borrowers to access funds against their home equity, subject to specific fees and conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0a48a482a40438f89f44e8758608310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8254e91bb361353c2efd5fd41f17e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd1c976503db6a0b9762d63aba656cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfcbc01d9662fc8a4930eb1a9dd46384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eec7e8fc248456d980c970b75e0fbf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662a2c10d200da7291e0212d33749544&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9351b24bca225d97ff2d45b46310a878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6</data>
