<node id="&quot;30 DAY SOFR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"30 Day SOFR (Secured Overnight Financing Rate) is a financial index used to calculate interest rates on certain financial products, indicating its importance in loan structuring."&lt;SEP&gt;"30 Day SOFR is a benchmark interest rate used in financial markets, specifically for the pricing of loans and derivatives, reflecting the cost of borrowing cash overnight secured by U.S. Treasury securities."&lt;SEP&gt;"30 Day SOFR, or 30-Day Secured Overnight Financing Rate, is a short-term interest rate used as a benchmark for certain adjustable-rate financial products."&lt;SEP&gt;"30 Day SOFR is a short-term interest rate index based on the Secured Overnight Financing Rate, used in financial products for variable interest rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"30 Day SOFR refers to the index used for variable interest rates in loans, based on the average of secured overnight financing transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b42b071e6198f2a53344eeed3e0dca2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f8738c76594c2ed9866d0e86818ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11f5ef3fffef89b593ca081411d1b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f2378deca7fb18f0144fa8707001424&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6d8750d3b8676bc5099fb262793a7ff</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 105}]</data>
</node>
