<node id="&quot;ESCROW WAIVER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"An Escrow Waiver is a request made by borrowers to waive the requirement of holding funds for tax and insurance within an escrow account."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow Waiver is a clause in the loan agreement that allows the borrower to forgo the standard escrow arrangement for property taxes and insurance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow Waiver is a financial term referring to a situation where funds typically held in escrow are waived, impacting loan processing details."&lt;SEP&gt;"Escrow Waiver is an agreement that allows a loan to close without establishing an escrow account, subject to specific approval."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1418f5447a956615e29938e7c6f0f71a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a577e8766cf4f0e1ae599795cd9c6fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73179b73b8a774ced8d562931d514540&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0908ef3e42a9d0bcd40742960e19dbf2</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 122}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 530}]</data>
</node>
