<node id="&quot;CONFORMING LOAN LIMIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL TERM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conforming Loan Limit is the maximum loan amount that government-sponsored enterprises will purchase, which varies by county and is a key parameter in the high loan amount programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conforming Loan Limit refers to the maximum mortgage amount that can be acquired through Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac, based on specific criteria and geographic limits."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conforming Loan Limit refers to the thresholds established for mortgage loans that can be purchased or backed by government-sponsored enterprises, which are recalibrated annually by FHFA."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Conforming Loan Limit sets a maximum loan amount that can be secured by loans that meet criteria set by the Federal Housing Finance Agency."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b75506a7175a05b7c26944fe1aa93eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1b06bf2c39f8da79b3399842638c80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc</data>
