<node id="&quot;LTV (LOAN-TO-VALUE)&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan-to-Value (LTV) is a financial term used to express the ratio of a loan to the value of an asset purchased, critical in risk assessment for mortgage applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan-to-Value is a ratio that compares the amount of the loan to the appraised value of the property, used by lenders to assess risk."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f1b06bf2c39f8da79b3399842638c80b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd0c5c971a5a48bbded5da8b256a175c</data>
