<node id="&quot;CONFORMING LOAN LIMITS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Conforming Loan Limits are established maximum amounts that lenders can offer for loans that are eligible for purchase by government-sponsored enterprises."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conforming Loan Limits are set by Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac to ensure that the loans they purchase or insure meet certain standards for eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conforming Loan Limits are the maximum loan amounts that Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac will back, ensuring loans meet eligibility requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conforming loan limits refer to the maximum borrowing amounts set for loans that meet specific guidelines, which vary based on property type and location."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conforming loan limits are the maximum loan amounts that can be purchased by Freddie Mac or Fannie Mae, affecting eligibility for standard mortgage products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Conforming Loan Limits are the maximum loan amounts set by the Federal Housing Finance Agency (FHFA) for loans eligible for purchase by Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-27bd5ad2c70145086339257520820a41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d3a76e6c1f50526ac6e8ed759d2710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4849d91ba0d105495fd48b0a77c7c582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3f42cc9266dff615db2fd5cb59e3109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f8738c76594c2ed9866d0e86818ca8</data>
