</node>
<node id="&quot;QUALIFYING RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Qualifying Rate is the interest rate used to calculate the borrower's financial capacity to repay the mortgage loan."&lt;SEP&gt;"Qualifying Rate refers to the interest rate applied to HELOCs that affects payment calculations and borrower qualifications based on the application date."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Qualifying Rate for HELOCs is determined by the fully indexed rate, affecting how eligibility for borrowing is assessed."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8df57131d49eba22a5ca15cafeb404cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1418f5447a956615e29938e7c6f0f71a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf</data>
