<node id="&quot;MORTGAGE LOAN PROGRAM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Mortgage Loan Program denotes specific types of loans offered to potential borrowers, detailed within the Guide, which include loans that are eligible for sale to Flagstar."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Loan Program is a term used to describe the various offerings for financing real estate transactions, including those that cater to jumbo loan amounts as specified in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Loan Program refers to the structured offerings of loans provided by lenders, available under various categories and terms to meet borrower needs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Loan Program refers to a specific type of loan designed with particular terms and conditions as described in the Guide, eligible for sale to Flagstar."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Loan Program refers to specific guidelines and criteria established for different types of mortgage loans available to borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortgage Loan Program refers to the set of guidelines and criteria established for evaluating and processing Mortgage Loans offered by the Seller."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Mortgage Loan Program outlines specific criteria and types of loans available to borrowers, with implications for underwriting and approval processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Mortgage Loan Program refers to the various structured programs available that govern the issuance and management of mortgage loans."</data>
