<node id="&quot;COOPERATIVE PROPERTIES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PROPERTY TYPE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cooperative Properties are homes owned by a corporation that owns the building, where residents buy shares rather than owning the real estate itself, rendering them ineligible under standard programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cooperative Properties refer to housing arrangements where residents own shares in a corporation that owns the building, which can complicate mortgage lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cooperative Properties refer to shared housing arrangements where residents own shares in a corporation that owns the property, often not eligible for conventional financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cooperative properties are listed as ineligible for HELOCs, indicating what types of ownership do not qualify for this financing option."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354a12aa9905401272b6367dbd3c30cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 65}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 360}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;HCLTV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"HCLTV (Home Equity Combined Loan-to-Value) is a measure used to evaluate the total amount of loans against a property’s value, relevant for refinancing options."&lt;SEP&gt;"HCLTV stands for Home Equity Combined Loan-To-Value, which takes into account the total of all loans against a property, relevant for assessing loan eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"HCLTV, or Home Equity Combined Loan-to-Value, reflects the maximum potential loan-to-value ratio when including home equity lines of credit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25dcfc163b5b00ffab734b755ea03592&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b943be84e7ac4bbf9b166f805ef17c</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 3}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 61}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 341}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 789}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXHIBIT A&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Exhibit A is a referenced document that includes detailed information regarding high-cost areas eligible for Freddie Mac financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exhibit A is referenced as a supplementary document containing a complete list of eligible locations and loan amount limits for mortgage products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exhibit A is a set of guidelines or a decision matrix relevant to the evaluation process for Standalone HELOCs, detailing various criteria for approval."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exhibit A is referred to as a Decision Matrix that must be completed prior to ordering property valuation products for standalone HELOCs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exhibit A refers to the Standalone HELOC Valuation Decision Matrix mentioned in the document as a supporting document for the Home Equity Line of Credit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-4a8254e91bb361353c2efd5fd41f17e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9c058471d343cfc8ca421fef3ff552d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a39b79f6d626310fd702e88ad4acda2b</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 112}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 494}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;5/6 SOFR ARM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"5/6 SOFR ARM refers to an Adjustable Rate Mortgage based on the secured overnight financing rate that adjusts after the initial fixed period of 5 years."</data>
