</node>
<node id="&quot;LTV/CLTV&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"MATHEMATICS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"LTV (Loan-to-Value) and CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) are metrics that lenders use to assess the risk of a mortgage loan relative to the property's value."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV/CLTV refers to Loan To Value/Combined Loan To Value, which are ratios used to assess the amount of the loan compared to the value of the property."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV (Loan-to-Value) and CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) are ratios that assess the risk of lending by comparing the loan amount to the appraised value of the property."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-94010f4bdf2ece06575cf539272b8b45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49a151d65e3cdee194b3d907f4671668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdba698a5ff7dd259797f2300b8f4759</data>
