<node id="&quot;ARM&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"ARM stands for Adjustable Rate Mortgage, a financing option described in the document for primary residence purchases and refinancing."&lt;SEP&gt;"ARM stands for Adjustable Rate Mortgage, a type of loan where the interest rate may change periodically, affecting the payments."&lt;SEP&gt;"ARM, or Adjustable Rate Mortgage, refers to a type of mortgage loan with an interest rate that can change periodically based on fluctuations in the market."&lt;SEP&gt;"ARM, or Adjustable Rate Mortgage, is a type of loan where the interest rate may change periodically based on changes in a corresponding financial index, as indicated in the loan comparisons."</data>
