  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Cooperative Property is a type of residential property where residents own shares in a corporation that owns the building, rather than owning their individual units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cooperative Property refers to a type of housing ownership where residents own shares in a corporation that owns the building, which can be subject to specific mortgage insurance products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cooperative Property refers to a type of housing where residents own shares in a cooperative corporation that owns the property, rather than owning their individual units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cooperative properties are residential properties owned by a corporation for which individuals can buy shares, but are ineligible under certain loan programs including Home Possible."</data>
