  <data key="d2">chunk-8c6c6dd97681ba9caa6c83d8ddf9ec59</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 8}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 111}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UPFRONT FEE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Upfront Fee is a charge that may be required in certain scenarios relating to loan locking commitments longer than 90 days."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8c6c6dd97681ba9caa6c83d8ddf9ec59</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DELIVERY CHOICE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Delivery Choice refers to the options available for how a locked loan must be delivered to Flagstar Bank, affecting processing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8c6c6dd97681ba9caa6c83d8ddf9ec59</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 113}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 496}, {"level": 3, "cluster": 828}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TIME DELIVERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Time Delivery denotes the expectations of timely submission of documents and loans as per the locked terms."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8c6c6dd97681ba9caa6c83d8ddf9ec59</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 126}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 536}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NOTICE OF CREDIT DENIAL&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Notice of Credit Denial is a document that may be provided by the correspondent in cases where the borrower withdraws their application."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-8c6c6dd97681ba9caa6c83d8ddf9ec59</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 10}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 135}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN DELIVERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Delivery entails submitting the required documents and funds needed to finalize a loan transaction before the expiration date."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Delivery is the process by which closed loans are submitted to Flagstar Bank, following specific delivery policies and timelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fff6b81ef8a66ecc49bb49ef81869a5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 126}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 535}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAIR-OFF&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Pair-Off is the scenario where a loan locked under mandatory commitment is subject to penalties if not delivered according to terms, affecting pricing and fees."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 22}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 223}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 769}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSTITUTION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Substitution is the process by which a correspondent may replace a loan that cannot be delivered under mandatory commitment with an approved loan of similar type."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 303}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOCK EXPIRATION DATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Lock Expiration Date indicates the date by which a loan must close or be locked in according to terms laid out by the lending institution."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 53}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKET CONDITIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Market Conditions refer to the current economic climate affecting interest rates and loan approvals, important for borrowers and lenders alike."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Conditions refer to the economic factors that can influence the rates, prices, and fees for mortgage products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Market Conditions refer to the various economic factors affecting real estate and mortgage lending, which impact the loan qualification process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b722d926669aa7676c36ecbb75a4a233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5c9771e9d7f170cab82a4f6e0fe9c6</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 1}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 29}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 244}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXTENSION GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Extension Guidelines are the set of rules governing how loans can be extended beyond their original terms when closing delays occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Extension Guidelines refer to the rules that dictate how loan extensions are managed after a lock period expires."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b722d926669aa7676c36ecbb75a4a233</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 53}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BEST EFFORTS DELIVERY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Best Efforts Delivery is a commitment type in which the correspondent agrees to deliver loans under reasonable circumstances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Best Efforts Delivery represents a more flexible delivery option for loans, focusing on achieving timely submission while accommodating market conditions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73179b73b8a774ced8d562931d514540</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 303}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MANDATORY COMMITMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Mandatory Commitment is a type of agreement where a correspondent must deliver specified loans to the lender as per agreed terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mandatory Commitment is a type of loan commitment requiring correspondents to fulfill delivery obligations as per the specified guidelines."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77f9a0c774af974e032ea5bf1841d2e</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 50}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 304}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN LOCK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Loan Lock is an agreement between a borrower and a lender that secures a specific interest rate for a loan for a determined period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan Lock refers to the agreement that locks in the loan's interest rate until a specified expiration date."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fff6b81ef8a66ecc49bb49ef81869a5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 9}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 126}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 535}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;WORSE CASE PRICING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Worse Case Pricing describes the pricing that would apply in a situation where previous float-downs have been executed, potentially leading to less favorable terms for further adjustments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Worse Case Pricing is a pricing mechanism employed when a loan is denied or rescinded, and it reflects the less favorable of two pricing options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Worse Case Pricing refers to the pricing strategy implemented when locks expire or certain conditions are not met, leading to potentially unfavorable terms for borrowers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Worse Case Pricing refers to the less favorable interest rate or terms that apply if a loan is delivered after its expiration date."&lt;SEP&gt;"Worse Case Pricing refers to potentially higher costs imposed if a required property address is not provided within necessary timelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Worse case pricing refers to the practice of setting loan terms based on the least favorable conditions to protect the lender's financial interests."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-fff6b81ef8a66ecc49bb49ef81869a5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b722d926669aa7676c36ecbb75a4a233&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77f9a0c774af974e032ea5bf1841d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af318020d8f16430d1a60515a789d41d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1afd5d25f6f318da0cbe2e55f0a46af0</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 22}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 223}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 769}]</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RATE CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"NORMAL_ENTITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Rate Change is the adjustment of the interest rate on a loan, which can affect the overall cost to the borrower."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75</data>
