<node id="&quot;DEBT-TO-INCOME RATIO&quot;">
  <data key="d2">&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8254e91bb361353c2efd5fd41f17e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ca1bd5008b14dffd1f24d89ce07116f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8df57131d49eba22a5ca15cafeb404cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f639d102461efe890e188cbc182dba52</data>
  <data key="d1">"Debt-To-Income Ratio is a financial metric used to assess an individual’s ability to manage monthly payments and repay debts, calculated by comparing debt payments to income."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio (DTI) is a measure of an individual's monthly debt payments compared to their gross monthly income, used to assess the borrower's ability to manage monthly payments on new debt."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio is a financial measure that compares a borrower's total monthly debt payments to their gross monthly income, crucial in evaluating HELOC eligibility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income ratio is a critical factor in determining qualifying ratios for loan applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Debt-to-Income Ratio (DTI) is a financial measure that compares a borrower's total monthly debt payments to their gross monthly income, helping lenders assess a borrower's ability to repay a loan."</data>
  <data key="d0">"FINANCIAL METRIC"</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 51}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 307}]</data>
</node>
