<node id="&quot;RIGHT OF RESCISSION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Right of Rescission is a guideline ensuring borrowers can cancel refinance transactions within a certain timeframe, relevant in the context of HELOC transactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Right of Rescission refers to the legal ability of borrowers to cancel a loan transaction within a specific timeframe, impacting their financial obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Right of Rescission is a legal provision allowing borrowers to cancel a credit transaction involving their primary dwelling within three business days after a triggering event, as mandated by Regulation Z and the federal Truth in Lending Law."&lt;SEP&gt;"Right of Rescission is a legal right that allows borrowers to cancel certain types of loans within a specific period, ensuring consumer protection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Right of Rescission is a legal provision allowing borrowers to cancel a transaction within a designated timeframe, emphasizing consumer protection."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Right of Rescission allows borrowers a set period to cancel the loan agreement after signing the necessary documents."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dc8b7db5bf49f6eb8f1e8daa83b6b361&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d99ce4642f1e6e8c39678043a90b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25a82bf13c8c6a8ef98d1a15a5361ea9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eec7e8fc248456d980c970b75e0fbf41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faf7af26dea16d8bcfcc9a3324ded2bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f5452ea8c1afd9252c54573e518675e</data>
