<node id="&quot;CONTINGENT FEES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Contingent Fees are fees charged by brokers that depend on specific conditions, such as the fulfillment of loan protocols and regulations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contingent Fees are fees that are applied contingent on certain conditions, such as a loan being underwritten and subsequently denied or withdrawn."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contingent Fees refer to charges that may apply based on specific conditions or actions, such as penalties or early payoff scenarios in the loan process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contingent fees are charges that are contingent upon certain conditions being met, particularly in the context of loan origination and servicing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contingent Fees pertain to additional charges that may apply under specific circumstances, as outlined in the document."&lt;SEP&gt;"Contingent Fees refer to a category of fees that are charged based on specific conditions related to loans and document processing, highlighting financial responsibilities involved in loan agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c0a48a482a40438f89f44e8758608310&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4b9e8302b8de2d8d692106e4e284ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1451e00f0a33296b7172a8a2f00a036&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42d99ce4642f1e6e8c39678043a90b1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-662a2c10d200da7291e0212d33749544&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f639d102461efe890e188cbc182dba52</data>
  <data key="d3">[{"level": 0, "cluster": 2}, {"level": 1, "cluster": 47}, {"level": 2, "cluster": 294}]</data>
</node>
