  <data key="d1">"Full Documentation is a method of income verification requiring extensive proof of a borrower's financial history over a two-year period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Full Documentation refers to the complete set of financial documents required for a mortgage application, demonstrating the borrower's income, assets, and creditworthiness."</data>
