  <data key="d1">"Cash Out denotes the transaction where a borrower refinances their mortgage for a larger amount than they owe, receiving the difference in cash."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cash Out refers to a type of refinancing where a borrower takes out cash against the equity in their home as part of the mortgage."</data>
