<edge source="&quot;FANNIE MAE&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">168.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both FANNIE MAE and FREDDIE MAC are government-sponsored enterprises that provide guidelines for the mortgage market."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both FANNIE MAE and FREDDIE MAC provide financing solutions for housing, including subordinate financing options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both FREDDIE MAC and FANNIE MAE are involved in the conforming loan limits and have standard loan documentation requirements."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac operate as government-sponsored enterprises in the housing market."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Both Freddie Mac and Fannie Mae are referenced as part of financial instruments related to mortgage products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac are both entities involved in the financing of properties through various loan programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac are both government-sponsored enterprises involved in the mortgage market, often issuing similar guidelines and products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac and Fannie Mae both operate within the government-sponsored enterprise framework to facilitate liquidity in the mortgage market, making them closely related."&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac is a counterpart to Fannie Mae, and both facilitate conventional loans in the secondary mortgage market."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac are both government-sponsored enterprises involved in the mortgage industry, providing standard mortgage financing options."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac are related entities that participate in similar market activities and products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac and Fannie Mae are both government-sponsored enterprises that operate in the mortgage market, supporting similar objectives and functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"FREDDIE MAC and FANNIE MAE are both major entities in the mortgage industry, directly competing and collaborating in various financial programs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac have similar objectives in promoting stability in the residential mortgage market, establishing a significant connection between them."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac's role in purchasing mortgages overlaps with Fannie Mae's mission to support mortgage credit availability, making them interrelated organizations in the financial sector."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Both entities are government-sponsored enterprises that provide support and services in the mortgage market."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac are both government-sponsored enterprises that impose certain guidelines and eligibility requirements for loans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Both Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac are government-sponsored enterprises that support the U.S. housing market."&lt;SEP&gt;"FANNIE MAE and FREDDIE MAC both outline standards for the mortgage industry, acting as key players in mortgage securitization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac operate under different guidelines but are both key players in the mortgage industry."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b75506a7175a05b7c26944fe1aa93eda&lt;SEP&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ae0a9048bf3b0256e59664fde5a07a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717a880d45de770514dc0429a3dc79f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72060811d2de811b03ec94848dcad94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef8667615745a5fec93f77636582f41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f28aa24c80be0008755d728b5169b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbc754fc30ff722a8fee09393323a03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44da442f8034719cd2f26599196416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f8738c76594c2ed9866d0e86818ca8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42979d97c1c73c1b28eac498c9aee682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29e2bb5014fcbf1d6e95d3ac5b1702bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a15606c9906902e66156e783e1ffe9b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48a2b2c8a98a031e15a7c52e9d1d96c6</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
