<edge source="&quot;LTV&quot;" target="&quot;CLTV/HCLTV&quot;">
  <data key="d4">52.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both LTV and CLTV/HCLTV are metrics used to assess the risk in mortgage lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV and CLTV/HCLTV calculations are crucial in determining overall loan limits for mortgages viewed by Fannie Mae."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV and CLTV/HCLTV metrics are essential in determining loan limits in Fannie Mae's guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV (Loan-to-Value) and CLTV/HCLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) are related metrics used in assessing mortgage eligibility and risk."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV and CLTV/HCLTV ratios are closely related as they determine the financing strategies for different property types."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV and CLTV/HCLTV are key financial metrics used in determining loan eligibility, showing their relationship in mortgage contexts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-92bc9ce80658e51e7fed2cac493270e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a33c29f8d16a498a486fa35e048c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61f35bbac411a48e356ef98016ff6b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ab83fcb34a1963a254e2dbce808acb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fafde8ee8a585c55ef0976f28ab4e55</data>
