<edge source="&quot;LTV&quot;" target="&quot;CLTV&quot;">
  <data key="d4">34.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Both LTV and CLTV are essential in determining the financial structure of mortgage loans and are interconnected metrics used during the loan process."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV (Loan-to-Value) and CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) are both essential metrics in evaluating mortgage eligibility, showing their interrelatedness."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV (Loan-to-Value) and CLTV (Combined Loan-to-Value) ratios are both crucial metrics in mortgage lending decisions, illustrating their close relationship."&lt;SEP&gt;"LTV and CLTV are both key metrics related to mortgage financing that assess loan to value ratios important for lenders."</data>
