<edge source="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;" target="&quot;FREDDIE MAC&quot;">
  <data key="d4">80.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Freddie Mac also provides mortgage solutions similar to Fannie Mae, aiming for liquidity in the housing market."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac and Fannie Mae both provide liquidity for the U.S. housing market and have comparable missions concerning mortgage loans."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac is a government-sponsored enterprise for the housing market, functioning alongside Fannie Mae."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac is directly referenced as an organization in the mortgage market, which fits within the context of mortgage insurance providers and their guidelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac itself is an organization providing financial assistance in the mortgage sector."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac is another entity that works closely with Fannie Mae in promoting stability in the mortgage market."&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac is closely related to Fannie Mae due to both being government-sponsored enterprises operating in the U.S. mortgage market to enhance credit availability."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac is similarly referred to as a government-sponsored enterprise also mentioned regarding loan waiver exceptions."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"Freddie Mac is the name of the organization referenced in the entity description."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
