</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ESCROW WAIVER&quot;" target="&quot;TAX PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">13.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Escrow waivers affect how tax payments are handled in loan transactions, establishing a relationship between the two terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The policies surrounding escrow waivers include conditions governing the payment of taxes, indicating an interdependent relationship."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9a577e8766cf4f0e1ae599795cd9c6fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ESCROW WAIVER&quot;" target="&quot;INSURANCE PAYMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If borrowers do not establish an escrow account, insurance payments cannot be rolled into the new loan, indicating a relationship governed by the escrow waiver rules."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9a577e8766cf4f0e1ae599795cd9c6fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ESCROW WAIVER&quot;" target="&quot;INSURANCE COVERAGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Borrowers are responsible for maintaining necessary insurance coverage, which is a requirement for the escrow waiver."&lt;</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9a577e8766cf4f0e1ae599795cd9c6fa</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
