  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Real Estate Syndication typically involves pooling resources for property investment, while a Revocable Living Trust may manage these pooled properties."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9351b24bca225d97ff2d45b46310a878</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXCEPTIONS TO TITLE&quot;" target="&quot;EASEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Easements are listed as exceptions to title, detailing specific exclusions from insurance coverage, thus connecting both concepts directly."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9351b24bca225d97ff2d45b46310a878</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EXCEPTIONS TO TITLE&quot;" target="&quot;ENCROACHMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Encroachments can be classified as exceptions to title, illustrating how physical property issues are recorded in the title insurance policy."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-9351b24bca225d97ff2d45b46310a878</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;EASEMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;EASEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Easements pertain specifically to the legal rights outlined in an easement agreement, which allows utilization of property for designated purposes."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENCROACHMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;PUBLIC UTILITY EASEMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Encroachments on public utility easements are regulated to ensure they do not interfere with public utilities while still allowing for certain exceptions."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e4823f54b9e7afeaec0c69de7747fd4e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENCROACHMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;TITLE POLICY ENDORSEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">9.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Endorsements to title policies often provide coverage against losses arising from encroachments on the property."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e4823f54b9e7afeaec0c69de7747fd4e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENCROACHMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;ENCROACHMENTS ON ADJOINING PROPERTY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Encroachments may occur on adjoining properties, impacting the use and enjoyment of the mortgaged premises."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e4823f54b9e7afeaec0c69de7747fd4e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENCROACHMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;PROPERTY LINE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Encroachments are often determined based on property lines, affecting ownership rights and usage."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e4823f54b9e7afeaec0c69de7747fd4e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;ENCROACHMENTS&quot;" target="&quot;EASEMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.5</data>
  <data key="d5">"Encroachments occur when structures intrude into easement areas, directly impacting the management of easement rights."</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;DEEDS OF TRUSTS&quot;" target="&quot;TRUSTEE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"A Trustee is responsible for managing the Deeds of Trust, linking personal responsibilities in trust management to real estate transactions."</data>
