  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"BEST EFFORTS DELIVERY relates to the assessment of a PAIR-OFF FEE when loans are closed and delivered to a different investor."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-73179b73b8a774ced8d562931d514540</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MANDATORY COMMITMENT&quot;" target="&quot;BEST-EFFORT COMMITMENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The text discusses how a loan under a best-effort commitment can be affected if denied, relating it directly to mandatory commitments."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e77f9a0c774af974e032ea5bf1841d2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;MANDATORY COMMITMENT&quot;" target="&quot;SUBSTITUTION GUIDELINES&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"The mandatory commitment requires adherence to substitution guidelines, establishing operational protocols in loan management."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e77f9a0c774af974e032ea5bf1841d2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;LOAN LOCK&quot;" target="&quot;RATE CHANGE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rate Change requests on locked Loans must be processed through the Lock Desk, impacting the Loan terms."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-c8b4e28d440c820b5ce2e89c08cd1b75</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORSE CASE PRICING&quot;" target="&quot;DENIED LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"If a loan is denied under a best-effort commitment, it becomes subject to worse case pricing if resubmitted."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e77f9a0c774af974e032ea5bf1841d2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORSE CASE PRICING&quot;" target="&quot;RESCINDED LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Rescinded loans see existing commitments become subject to worse case pricing if resubmitted, linking both concepts closely."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e77f9a0c774af974e032ea5bf1841d2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORSE CASE PRICING&quot;" target="&quot;LOCKED-IN RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Worse case pricing is compared with the locked-in rate to determine unfavorable outcomes, showcasing their relationship in loan pricing."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-e77f9a0c774af974e032ea5bf1841d2e</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORSE CASE PRICING&quot;" target="&quot;LOCK COMMITMENT EXPIRED&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"WORSE CASE PRICING applies to loans once their LOCK COMMITMENT has expired, affecting the cost structure."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-fff6b81ef8a66ecc49bb49ef81869a5f</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORSE CASE PRICING&quot;" target="&quot;FLOAT-DOWN RENEGOTIATION POLICY&quot;">
  <data key="d4">7.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"FLOAT-DOWN RENEGOTIATION POLICY specifies WORSE CASE PRICING applies to re-locks after a float-down."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-af318020d8f16430d1a60515a789d41d</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORSE CASE PRICING&quot;" target="&quot;LOCK PERIOD EXTENSION&quot;">
  <data key="d4">8.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"WORSE CASE PRICING applies when a LOCK PERIOD EXTENSION is not timely managed, showcasing their connection in the pricing and extension process."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-b722d926669aa7676c36ecbb75a4a233</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="&quot;WORSE CASE PRICING&quot;" target="&quot;COMMITMENT REQUIREMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d4">6.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"Commitment requirements can be affected by worse case pricing if a loan application is resubmitted after being declined, linking the two concepts."</data>
  <data key="d6">chunk-1afd5d25f6f318da0cbe2e55f0a46af0</data>
  <data key="d7">1</data>
</edge>
